{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_137","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cmp cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv \"$TMPDIR/divider.fKcA2BBY/carry/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\" && git diff --check && git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n# Trailing radix-4 divider trials\n\nEach round consumes dividend bits from the MSB in groups of (1, 2, 2) in the 4-bit lane, (2, 2) in the 11-bit lane, and (1, 2) in the 18-bit lane. The 25-bit and 32-bit lanes use two and one binary restores per round, respectively.\n\nAt issue, the divider registers three times the low 18 bits of the divisor magnitude in 20 bits. Each paired trial subtracts D, 2D, and 3D in parallel. The comparison against 2D selects between the two lower and two upper remainder candidates. The divider retains its prefix seeds, seven-round schedule, signed correction, divide-by-zero result, and result-hold behavior.\n\nThe D trial checks the two high bits of the shifted remainder in parallel with a W-bit subtraction. The 2D trial compares the shifted remainder above bit zero against D and passes bit zero directly to the candidate remainder. The 3D trial uses the proposed W+3-bit subtraction. These width reductions retain the full-precision borrow decisions and saved 43 Gowin logic cells compared with writing all three trials at full width.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with zero warnings.\n- Local riscv-formal passed all 53 checks with the single-retirement wrapper and ALTOPS on the first run.\n- All 23 ALU tests and both multiplier tests passed.\n- An SMT check of the synthesized RTL proved that issue captures the correct 3D value and that it holds between issues. For each of the three narrow lanes, a round produced the same quotient and remainder as serial binary restores for every nonzero divisor fitting the lane, every incoming remainder below that divisor, and arbitrary quotient-register contents.\n- Co-simulation passed on selftest and three random programs, each with and without memory stalls. The stalled CoreMark run matched all five canonical CRCs and completed ten iterations in 3,044,309 marker cycles.\n\n## Local timing\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 83.656, 92.229, and 92.229 MHz using 4,936 logic cells and 1,934 registers. The 92.229 MHz median gives 302.96 CoreMark iterations/s, 8.50% above 279.21. Only placement 0 fell below the stated 88.91 MHz threshold. In the median placement the longest setup path runs from the registered EX/MEM ALU result to the EX operand register.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
