{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Radix-16 combinational divider\n\nDIV, DIVU, REM and REMU share eight combinational digit stages in EX. Each stage appends four dividend bits and subtracts 15 shared divisor multiples in parallel. Adjacent fit flags select the largest fitting multiple's residual, including the original trial for digit zero. The quotient and remainder share the final sign correction.\n\nThe first two stages precompute whether each multiple fits the trial width by comparing the divisor with the constant `floor((2^W - 1) / k)`. This lets those stages start before the high bits of the 36-bit multiples settle. The other six stages test the upper bits directly. With a zero divisor every digit is 15 and the residual reproduces the dividend magnitude. Suppressing quotient negation in that case gives the RV32M all-ones quotient. The 32-bit magnitude path also gives the specified result for `INT_MIN / -1`.\n\n## Local results\n\n| Measure | Baseline | Radix-16 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Gowin placement 0, MHz | 5.140 | 7.382 |\n| Gowin placement 1, MHz | 5.442 | 7.774 |\n| Gowin placement 2, MHz | 5.442 | 7.774 |\n| CoreMark cycles between markers | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 |\n| CoreMark iterations/s at median clock | 12.12 | 17.31 |\n| Gowin logic cells, placement 0 | 12,312 | 7,354 |\n\nThe divider remains on the critical path. Placement 0 reports a 140.753 ns worst arrival through forwarding and the EX ALU to data memory.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator passed the requested wildcard lint command with `-Wall`. A guarded include makes the core declarations available in that file order.\n- Local formal passed all 53 checks on the first run of the final RTL. The fast suite used the existing ALTOPS equations. Cocotb and cosimulation checked the hardware arithmetic.\n- All 81 cocotb tests passed. Three new tests made 14,620 exact comparisons across the four division operations, covering digit thresholds at every nibble position, divisor-width boundaries, signed extrema, zero divisors and seeded random operands.\n- Cosimulation passed for five ELFs. The selftest and three random programs matched the ISS both with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed all five CRCs and printed “Correct operation validated.” Its start and stop markers were at cycles 15,801 and 4,507,286.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
