{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat tools/eval/_slots.py; command -v riscv32-unknown-elf-gcc; cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; ls -ld /sys/fs/cgroup /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu*; rg -n 'implementation_notes.md' tools/tournament.py tools/sandbox.py\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Host-wide slots for the harness's heavy evals (formal, Gowin builds).\n\nThree concurrent runs, each evaluating up to three slots, plus the agents'\nown self-checks, saturated the 20-core run host (load 20); formal checks then\nhit their wall-clock ceiling because of what other runs were doing, not\nbecause of the design (V2.1 campaign, first batch). With HARNESS_EVAL_SLOTS\nset, each eval holds one of that many flock'ed slots (in HARNESS_EVAL_LOCK_DIR,\noperator-only) for its duration, and its timeout starts once it holds one.\nUnset (agents' own `make timing`, tests): no limit. The variables use a prefix\nthe agent environment does not inherit (tools/agents/_runtime.py).\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport contextlib\nimport fcntl\nimport os\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\n@contextlib.contextmanager\ndef eval_slot(what: str = \"eval\"):\n    n = int(os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_SLOTS\", \"0\") or 0)\n    lock_dir = os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_LOCK_DIR\", \"\")\n    if n <= 0 or not lock_dir:\n        yield\n        return\n    d = Path(lock_dir)\n    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    started, told = time.time(), False\n    while True:\n        for i in range(n):\n            f = open(d / f\"slot{i}.lock\", \"w\")\n            try:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n            except BlockingIOError:\n                f.close()\n                continue\n            waited = time.time() - started\n            if waited > 60:\n                print(f\"  [eval] {what}: got host eval slot {i} after {waited:.0f}s\", flush=True)\n            try:\n                yield\n            finally:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n                f.close()\n            return\n        if not told:\n            print(f\"  [eval] {what}: waiting for a host eval slot ({n} busy)\", flush=True)\n            told = True\n        time.sleep(5)\n\n\ndef eval_jobs(default: str | None = None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"make -j for a formal run holding a slot (HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS).\"\"\"\n    return os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS\") or default\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/bin/riscv32-unknown-elf-gcc\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r1s0 (regression, +42.82%): Testing 15 divisor multiples in parallel raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 7.774 MHz, but chaining eight radix-16 remainder selections in one EX cycle kept the core below the multicycle divider's 43.9 MHz.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r1s1 (improvement, +705.78%): Registering the shared EX divider after every six restoring steps shortened the critical path, and CoreMark incurred no divide stalls because it executed no DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU between timing markers.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.76%): Predicting branches with 32 two-bit counters and steering JALs in fetch avoided one-cycle EX redirects and cut CoreMark cycles by 6.4%, but the combinational EX divider kept Fmax near 5.5 MHz versus 43.9 MHz with multicycle division.\ndr-xr-xr-x 13 nobody nogroup 0 Sep 28 22:33 /sys/fs/cgroup\n-rw-r--r--  1 nobody nogroup 0 Nov 19 16:42 /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.pressure\n-r--r--r--  1 nobody nogroup 0 Nov 19 16:42 /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.stat\n-r--r--r--  1 nobody nogroup 0 Nov 19 16:42 /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.stat.local\n-r--r--r--  1 nobody nogroup 0 Nov 19 16:42 /sys/fs/cgroup/cpuset.cpus.effective\n-r--r--r--  1 nobody nogroup 0 Nov 19 16:42 /sys/fs/cgroup/cpuset.cpus.isolated\n-r--r--r--  1 nobody nogroup 0 Nov 19 16:42 /sys/fs/cgroup/cpuset.mems.effective\ntools/sandbox.py:100:    if path in _KEEP_IGNORED or path == \"implementation_notes.md\":\ntools/sandbox.py:102:    if target and