{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Divider implementation\n\nEX still takes six rounds. Divisor magnitudes from 1 through 4095 use five restoring trials per round, each with a 12-bit restored remainder, a 13-bit shifted value, and a borrow bit. Larger divisors seed the remainder from the top twelve dividend bits and consume three bits per round. A divisor of at least 2³⁰ bypasses the EX subtractors. For division by zero, each wide trial succeeds and reconstructs the dividend for REM and REMU. Both paths hand off after dividend bit 2 to the existing two-bit MEM tail.\n\nOnly narrow mode reads quotient slots 29 through 18, so those slots always shift by five. This removes twelve shift-selection muxes from the proposed design. In wide mode, MEM supplies twelve leading quotient bits from the latched divide-by-zero flag.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- All 53 single-channel riscv-formal checks passed on the final RTL without retries. This gate uses ALTOPS. The cocotb tests exercise the hardware divider arithmetic.\n- All 99 cocotb cases passed. The new test exercises all four division and remainder instructions at divisor magnitudes 4095, 4096, and 4097, including signed operand combinations, mixed octal quotient digits, all four dividend tails, exact multiples, and remainders one below the divisor. Back-to-back issues use the existing six-round and result-hold checks.\n- Co-simulation passed the self-test and three randomized programs against the ISS in both bus-stall configurations. With both stalls enabled, ten CoreMark iterations took 3,399,350 marker cycles and passed the canonical CRC and UART checks.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement option | Fmax |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 54.925 MHz |\n| 1 | 55.994 MHz |\n| 2 | 55.994 MHz |\n\nThe 55.994 MHz median gives **164.72 iterations/s**, 8.92% above the 151.23 iterations/s baseline. Option 0 used 3,930 logic cells and 956 registers. Its worst setup path starts in the fetch-stage successor RAM. The worst paths for options 1 and 2 start at the ID/EX source-register address.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
