{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_164","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Decode-time register dependencies\n\nDecode compares each source register with all three older destinations. The ID/EX enable captures the youngest tag match, the qualified MEM match, the WB and register-file fallback selects, and one shared copy of WB data. In EX, the youngest match wins only when EX/MEM permits the write and the memory access is aligned. A faulting load or jump therefore exposes the next eligible source. Each operand uses a four-source masked OR. The youngest select also drives the load-to-branch and pointer-load bypasses.\n\nThe register file uses unreset distributed RAM with a resettable written bit for each of x1 through x31. In the core, an all-zero operand mask supplies zero for x0 and unwritten registers. The standalone register file retains same-cycle write-through on both read ports.\n\n## Divider timing\n\nThe forwarding change alone measured 61.471 MHz median. Gowin reported the narrow-divisor restoring chain and the two serial final quotient bits among the longest paths. The implementation adds a six-bit lane for divisors below 64 and resolves the last two quotient bits together by comparing against D, 2D and 3D. The registered divisor supplies the lane enables and the triple multiple during the six restoring rounds. Issue capture, divide latency and the result handshake follow the existing schedule.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe target declares `nret: 1` in `core.yaml`. Local validation uses its single-retirement RVFI wrapper. The ALTOPS formal suite checks the forwarding and retirement logic. The ALU tests exercise real signed and unsigned division, including the new lane boundary and overflow of the final trial multiples. Pipeline tests cover consecutive trapping writers falling back to the shared issue-edge WB value and to raw register-file data. The register-file reset test writes all writable rows before resetting them.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
