{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_209","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md | tail -13'","aggregated_output":"## Verification\n\nThe target declares `nret: 1` in `core.yaml`. Local validation uses its single-retirement RVFI wrapper. The ALTOPS formal suite checks the forwarding and retirement logic. The ALU tests exercise real signed and unsigned division, including the new lane boundary and overflow of the final trial multiples. Pipeline tests cover consecutive trapping writers falling back to the shared issue-edge WB value and to raw register-file data. The register-file reset test writes all writable rows before resetting them.\n\n- Strict Verilator lint passed. All 102 cocotb tests passed.\n- Selftest and the three random RVFI traces matched the ISS with ready buses and with both buses stalled.\n- CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,223,900 bracketed cycles, from cycle 12,291 to 3,236,191. The UART reported `Correct operation validated.` and CRCs `e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a` and `fcaf`. The simulator reported no out-of-bounds access.\n\n## FPGA result\n\nGowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 64.366, 66.918 and 66.918 MHz. The median exceeds the 63.5356 MHz threshold and yields 207.57 CoreMark iterations/s.\n\nThe design uses 4,118 logic cells and 1,242 registers, increases of 237 cells and 52 registers over the parent in `core.yaml`. Gowin inferred 32 distributed-RAM blocks for the register file. The full design uses 13 block RAMs and 2 DSPs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
