{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_163", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'du -sh cores/bench/generated/timing*; git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "34M\tcores/bench/generated/timing\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_addr\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_addr_compare\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_addr_compare_div\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_compare\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_div_payload\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_forward\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_normal_pc\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_recovered_pc\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_stage_recovery\n12M\tcores/bench/generated/timing_target_sum\n M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n# Registered replay recovery\n\nIF uses the registered recovery bit on the cycle that it presents the redirect target. It suppresses the buffered word and the outstanding row, issues a ready external word immediately, and starts a sequential RAM read. A stalled fetch retains the buffer only on a qualified hit, so a discarded word cannot reappear on the next cycle. FENCE.I still clears the group validity mask. A simultaneous fill and read of the same row still suppresses that response.\n\nEX/MEM holds its payload during data backpressure. Reset and divide bubbles clear retirement validity, forwarding permission, and both memory enables. MEM/WB holds the preceding writer during a data wait and clears retirement validity, allowing collection to use the value throughout the wait. Reset clears its writer permission.\n\n## Timing-driven changes\n\nThe replay and bubble changes alone measured 71.917 MHz median. The worst paths still reached the data RAM address and the recovered PC. The following changes preserve the issue and retirement schedule.\n\n- EX/MEM has a dedicated data address. The additions for the saved base, adjacent ALU result, and forwarded load run in parallel. MEM uses the registered address for alignment, lane selection, and the bus request.\n- For a load-dependent BEQ or BNE, MEM compares the unshifted RAM bytes against the other operand. The byte mask selects the participating lanes, and a separate check verifies the sign or zero extension.\n- With those two changes, the divide result register limited placement 1 at 74.572 MHz. The seventh round already stores the final quotient and remainder in each lane. MEM now selects those registers directly, before the next divide can overwrite them. The divider retains its seven rounds and its existing transfer handshake.\n\n## Local checks\n\nVerilator lint passed without warnings. The single-channel ALTOPS formal gate passed all 53 checks on the first run of the final RTL. All six cocotb suites passed, including the real divider arithmetic and pipeline tests. Selftest and the three random programs matched the ISS on every retirement with and without stalls.\n\nA separate comparison of two complete dividers hit its 90-second SAT limit. Sharing the identical round logic allowed induction to prove that the two result-selection circuits agree whenever a completed result is available to MEM, including through backpressure.\n\nCoreMark completed ten iterations with both bus stalls in 3,273,911 bracketed cycles. The start and stop markers were at cycles 12,762 and 3,286,673. All five canonical CRCs and the validation banner matched, and the harness reported no out-of-bounds access.\n\n## Measured timing\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 78.039, 76.247, and 76.247 MHz. The median clears the 74.799 MHz qualifying frequency by 1.448 MHz and yields 232.89 CoreMark iterations per second. The placed design uses 4,276 logic cells and 1,488 registers, increases of 159 and 12 over the starting design.\n\nThe limiting path on placements 1 and 2 runs from the registered adjacent rs1 match through EX to the ID/EX valid register, with an arrival time of 18.410 ns.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
