{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; git check-ignore -v cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_multiplier.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\tcores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Forward the low multiply result from EX/MEM\n\nEX computes one signed 33-by-33 product from the forwarded register operands. Operand collection prepares the sign-extension bits from the youngest available values. A high multiply waits one cycle for an adjacent source writer. MUL uses zero extension and can consume either or both inputs from the adjacent bypass.\n\nMutually exclusive masks select the low product, jump link or base ALU result into the existing EX/MEM bypass register. EX/MEM also captures the upper product. Both registers hold during data-bus backpressure. MEM selects the upper word for MULH, MULHSU and MULHU and uses that selection for forwarding and writeback. The implementation follows the proposed schedule.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed. All 53 single-retire ALTOPS formal checks passed on the first run.\n- All six cocotb suites passed. The multiplier oracle checks the low word for every signedness configuration. Pipeline tests check exact retirement gaps, RVFI operands and results, both source positions, double matches, x0, a load hold and a flushed multiply.\n- Selftest and all three random programs matched the ISS with and without bus stalls. A separate 5,297-retirement trace of dependent products, loads, stores and branches matched the ISS with both stalls enabled.\n- Stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,238,429 marker cycles, saving 35,482 cycles. All five canonical CRCs and the validation banner matched.\n\n## FPGA timing\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 79.624, 82.325 and 82.325 MHz. The median yields **254.21 iterations/s**, 6.25% above the 239.26 baseline and above the 250.27 acceptance floor. Placement 0 used 4,045 LUT4s, 1,435 flip-flops and two DSPs. Divider feedback limits the clock at the median placement.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
