{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_216","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'radix|restoring|g_lane' cores/bench/rtl || true; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Reciprocal division with the shared EX multiplier\n\nThe 1,024 × 49-bit synchronous ROM supplies a reciprocal endpoint and slope. A 17 × 13-bit multiply interpolates the reciprocal. Rounds three and five write unsigned factors into the held EX operand registers and clear their adjacent bypasses. Round four samples the high word of A×M and round six retains 33 bits of E×D.\n\nThe divider detects M = 2³² during normalization, when the ROM index and truncated fraction are both zero. It precomputes A+D and E−1. Complementing both operands of the final subtraction restores negative results. REM by zero uses P = 0 and restores the dividend sign. Round seven updates the architectural result register, which holds its value through backpressure and the next issue.\n\nCollection qualifies the multiplier's left operand and its adjacent bypass. The low product feeds the EX result OR directly. Division keeps its original forwarded operands for RVFI. Independent divides retire eight cycles apart and dependent low multiplies can retire on adjacent cycles.\n\n## Measurements\n\n| Gowin placement | Fmax |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 86.229 MHz |\n| 1 | 86.950 MHz |\n| 2 | 86.950 MHz |\n\nThe median is 0.330 MHz below the 87.28 MHz hypothesis target. At 3,238,429 bracketed cycles for ten CoreMark iterations, this gives 268.49 iterations/s. The median placement's worst path runs from data RAM to the fetch recovery PC. Gowin reports 3,844 logic cells, 1,527 registers, 18 block RAMs and two DSPs, including the shared 36 × 36 multiplier and the 18 × 18 interpolation multiplier.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The single-retirement ALTOPS formal gate passed all 53 checks with zero failures. The preprocessed RTL matched the staged proof input byte for byte.\n- Verilator lint passed in both real-arithmetic and ALTOPS configurations. All 1,024 elaborated ROM rows matched independently calculated integer coefficients.\n- The arithmetic tests check every exponent and every ROM row, including endpoints, midpoints, neighbors, exact multiples and off-by-one dividends. They also check a correction with P above 2³², result retention and resets during a divide.\n- The pipeline tests check RVFI operands, shared multiplier forwarding, an independent ADD after a divide, and divide spacing under instruction and data waits.\n- Co-simulation matched selftest and three random retirement traces against the ISS with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark produced CRCs e9f5, e714, 1fd7, 8e3a and fcaf and printed “Correct operation validated.”\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
