{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat Makefile; cat formal/run_all.sh'", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[15174 of 18246 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1a4156bac2e0e834]…\nheses make the assumption satisfiable, so this\n        # branch never matches and the regular DONE (PASS branch covers it.\n        PASS=$((PASS+1))\n    else\n        FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); FAILED+=(\"$name\")\n    fi\ndone\nTOTAL=$((PASS+FAIL))\nif [ $TOTAL -eq 0 ]; then\n    FAIL=1\n    FAILED+=(\"no_checks_generated\")\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Formal: $PASS passed, $FAIL failed\"\nif [ $FAIL -gt 0 ]; then\n    echo \"Failed: ${FAILED[*]}\"\n    # Surface the FIRST failing check's logfile tail. tools/eval/formal.py\n    # captures this script's stdout/stderr into formal['detail'] and the\n    # orchestrator now records that in experiments/log.jsonl, so what we\n    # print here is what shows up as the diagnostic for the failed run.\n    first=\"${FAILED[0]}\"\n    if [ -f \"$first/logfile.txt\" ]; then\n        echo \"\"\n        echo \"--- $first/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\"\n        tail -30 \"$first/logfile.txt\"\n    fi\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"Full run log: $LOG\"\n    echo \"Per-check logs in: $CORE_DIR/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\"\nfi\n[ $FAIL -eq 0 ]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/core.sv; cat cores/bench/test/conftest.py; rg -n 'implementation_notes' .gitignore CLAUDE.md; rg --files tools/eval test/cosim cores/bench/test\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/core.sv; cat cores/bench/test/conftest.py; rg -n 'implementation_notes' .gitignore CLAUDE.md; rg --files tools/eval test/cosim cores/bench/test\"", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/core.sv\n//\n// Top-level wiring for the 5-stage in-order RV32IM core.\n//\n//  IF -> ID -> EX -> MEM -> WB\n//   |    |     ^\n//   |    +-----+    forward_unit drives EX-stage rs1/rs2 muxes\n//   |               from EX/MEM and MEM/WB\n//   +- stall <- hazard_unit (load-use)\n//\n// IO port names use the `io_*` Chisel-emit prefix so the existing\n// formal/wrapper_si.sv and test/cosim/main.cpp bindings carry through\n// byte-for-byte. RVFI port set is the single-channel set described in\n// CLAUDE.md invariant 1 under `nret: 1` (declared in core.yaml). The\n// orchestrator routes formal to wrapper_si.sv + checks_si.cfg and FPGA\n// synth to fpga/core_bench_si.sv for this core. There is no channel 1.\n//\n// Latency:        full pipeline; instruction n retires at MEM/WB on\n//                 cycle n+4 (no hazards) or later (load-use stall,\n//                 redirect).\n// RVFI fields:    all of them — driven from the MEM/WB register and\n//                 the WB-stage write-data mux.\nmodule core (\n  input  logic        clock,\n  input  logic        reset,\n  // imem\n  output logic [31:0] io_imemAddr,\n  input  logic [31:0] io_imemData,\n  // A BTB hit can supply the instruction while imem is stalled.\n  input  logic        io_imemReady,\n  // dmem\n  output logic [31:0] io_dmemAddr,\n  input  logic [31:0] io_dmemRData,\n  output logic [31:0] io_dmemWData,\n  output logic [3:0]  io_dmemWEn,\n  output logic        io_dmemREn,\n  // dmem bus backpressure. Drive 1 for zero-wait. Drive 0 to model\n  // dStall — when there is a memory op in EX/MEM, the entire pipeline\n  // freezes back to MEM; MEM/WB captures a bubble; the LOAD/STORE waits\n  // until the bus delivers.\n  input  logic        io_dmemReady,\n  // RVFI — single-channel retirement port set (NRET=1 contract,\n  // declared via `nret: 1` in core.yaml). Channel 0 is the sole\n  // retirement channel. See CLAUDE.md invariant 1 for the full contract.\n  output logic        io_rvfi_valid_0,\n  output logic [63:0] io_rvfi_order_0,\n  output logic [31:0] io_rvfi_insn_0,\n  output logic        i\n…[6660 of 9732 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a4dc881f92bca233]…\n`\nCLAUDE.md:59:lives at `cores/<TARGET>/implementation_notes.md` (gitignored). The\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ntest/cosim/reference.py\ntest/cosim/main.cpp\ntest/cosim/build.sh\ntest/cosim/run_cosim.py\ntools/eval/_slots.py\ntools/eval/cosim.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_nret.py\ntools/eval/test_fpga_report.py\ntools/eval/holdout.py\ntools/eval/gowin.py\ntools/eval/formal.py\ntools/eval/test_gate_sanity.py\ntools/eval/_subprocess.py\ntools/eval/test_holdout.py\ntools/eval/fpga.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_workdir_cleanup.py\ntools/eval/test_rvfi_lint.py\ntools/eval/test_process_reaper.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_reclassify.py\ntools/eval/rvfi_lint.py\ntools/eval/test_remove_path.py\ntools/eval/test_subprocess_pgroup.py\ntools/eval/__init__.py\ntools/eval/test_slots.py\ntools/eval/test_bench_stall_gen.py\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
