{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'du -shL formal/riscv-formal/checks formal/riscv-formal/insns && cat formal/checks_si.cfg && ls -a formal/riscv-formal && cat tools/eval/_slots.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'du -shL formal/riscv-formal/checks formal/riscv-formal/insns && cat formal/checks_si.cfg && ls -a formal/riscv-formal && cat tools/eval/_slots.py'", "aggregated_output": "996K\tformal/riscv-formal/checks\n4.5M\tformal/riscv-formal/insns\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n.\n..\n.agents\n.aws\n.codex\n.git\n.github\n.gitignore\n.mailmap\n.readthedocs.yaml\nCOPYING\nCodeOfConduct\nREADME.md\nbus\nchecks\ncores\ndocs\ninsns\nmonitor\ntests\n\"\"\"Host-wide slots for the harness's heavy evals (formal, Gowin builds).\n\nThree concurrent runs, each evaluating up to three slots, plus the agents'\nown self-checks, saturated the 20-core run host (load 20); formal checks then\nhit their wall-clock ceiling because of what other runs were doing, not\nbecause of the design (V2.1 campaign, first batch). With HARNESS_EVAL_SLOTS\nset, each eval holds one of that many flock'ed slots (in HARNESS_EVAL_LOCK_DIR,\noperator-only) for its duration, and its timeout starts once it holds one.\nUnset (agents' own `make timing`, tests): no limit. The variables use a prefix\nthe agent environment does not inherit (tools/agents/_runtime.py).\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport contextlib\nimport fcntl\nimport os\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\n@contextlib.contextmanager\ndef eval_slot(what: str = \"eval\"):\n    n = int(os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_SLOTS\", \"0\") or 0)\n    lock_dir = os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_LOCK_DIR\", \"\")\n    if n <= 0 or not lock_dir:\n        yield\n        return\n    d = Path(lock_dir)\n    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    started, told = time.time(), False\n    while True:\n        for i in range(n):\n            f = open(d / f\"slot{i}.lock\", \"w\")\n            try:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n            except BlockingIOError:\n                f.close()\n                continue\n            waited = time.time() - started\n            if waited > 60:\n                print(f\"  [eval] {what}: got host eval slot {i} after {waited:.0f}s\", flush=True)\n            try:\n                yield\n            finally:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n                f.close()\n            return\n        if not told:\n            print(f\"  [eval] {what}: waiting for a host eval slot ({n} busy)\", flush=True)\n            told = True\n        time.sleep(5)\n\n\ndef eval_jobs(default: str | None = None) -> str