eed only 15-bit trial subtractors and seeding the wide remainder with the top 14 dividend bits cuts the 33-bit subtractor chain from six to three per round.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 (improvement, +9.91%): Storing the control-transfer instruction word in the 64-entry BTB let a tag h\n…[5454 of 8526 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d8561376296ef214]…\n0261121-002-r9s1 (improvement, +9.54%): Registering per-source bypass enables during producer EX removed `EX/MEM.mem_read` from the next address calculation, and comparing active RAM bytes in parallel with an extension check on the other operand let dependent BEQ/BNE resolve without waiting for load formatting.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r9s2 (regression, +5.88%): Looking up load words during operand collection let adjacent branches and pointer loads use a registered operand in EX while MEM verified the hit, but the prototype’s 4.1% reduction in CoreMark cycles could not offset its lower median Fmax relative to the round winner (72.784 vs 78.330 MHz).\n\"\"\"pytest configuration for cocotb unit tests.\n\nAdds this directory to sys.path so test_*.py modules can `import _helpers`\nduring pytest collection. Cocotb sets PYTHONPATH separately for the\nsimulator-side import.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n_HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nif str(_HERE) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HERE))\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
