{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_154","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; cat /proc/loadavg; ls -lh formal/last_run-* | tail -6'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/load_predictor.sv\n# Resident-page load prediction\n\nCollection launches a synchronous word read using a predicted base and a split displacement sum. The base can come from the previous load's raw word. EX uses the forwarded address to format that candidate and starts an exact-address retry. MEM checks the registered eligibility bits and selects the early word, retry word, or accepted bus response. A failed prediction holds an adjacent consumer in EX and repairs every matching source before execution resumes.\n\nThe resident page has 1,024 byte-writable words, per-word initialization and a full-sector bit for each group of eight words. A RAM reference establishes the initial page. The 32nd consecutive reference to the same competing page replaces it. Stored validity, held probes and pending fills follow page changes and reset. Partial stores preserve word validity. Both probes exclude collisions with physical writes and logically completed older writes.\n\nThe single write-through slot absorbs an ordinary store when the bus stalls. An available bus can accept a store directly. The bus address has its own register so Gowin can infer block RAM in the timing wrapper. RVFI uses the retiring operation's address, mask and raw load word. The core retains the single retirement channel declared in core.yaml.\n\nJALR verification compares the upper 31 bits of rs1 with two expected bases calculated in collection. The architectural sum still supplies alignment, recovery and RVFI. 