{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Predict register writes before the alignment check\n\nEX now advertises a valid decoded register writer to operand collection while it checks alignment. When an instruction advances with a link or data alignment fault, EX redirects to PC+4. Refetch lets the consumer collect the youngest surviving register value. The faulting instruction retires once with its trap, and its fault-qualified control suppresses register and memory writes and memory reads.\n\nThe RTL follows the proposed two control changes. The pipeline tests check that an aligned load with a dependent consumer takes one repair cycle and that successors of misaligned loads, jumps, and stores retire three clocks after the fault. The store case extends the forwarded-address test to cover recovery when the faulting instruction has no destination register.\n\nThe backpressure regression holds a cold LW for five data waits while a misaligned LH to the same x5 is in EX. It checks one accepted read, one trapped LH, and one accepted SW carrying the LW value of `0x87654321`.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- All 53 single-retirement ALTOPS formal checks passed on the first run.\n- All 46 pipeline tests passed, along with the ALU, decoder, immediate generator, multiplier, and register file suites.\n- Selftest and all three random programs matched the ISS with and without stalls.\n- CoreMark completed ten iterations with both stall generators in 3,044,309 marker cycles. All five canonical CRCs and the validation banner matched.\n\n## Timing and area\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 94.763, 97.260, and 97.260 MHz. The median yields **319.48 iterations/s**, a **5.45% gain** over the 92.229 MHz champion at the same marker cycle count. The design uses 4,883 logic cells, 1,934 registers, 25 BSRAMs, and two DSPs.\n\nAlignment faults cost two refetch cycles even when the successor is independent. That cost did not change the CoreMark marker interval.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
