{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'ls -la formal && cat formal/checks_si.cfg && ls -la /opt/gowin && cat /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max && cat /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max'","aggregated_output":"total 56\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 21 14:19 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 21 14:20 ..\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2630 Nov 21 14:19 checks-deep.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2658 Nov 21 14:19 checks.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  1455 Nov 21 14:19 checks_si.cfg\nlrwxrwxrwx+  1 nobody nogroup    68 Nov 21 14:19 riscv-formal -> /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep4/formal/riscv-formal\n-rwxrwx---+  1 nobody nogroup 10597 Nov 21 14:19 run_all.sh\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  4615 Nov 21 14:19 wrapper.sv\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2863 Nov 21 14:19 wrapper_si.sv\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\ntotal 24\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul 10  2025 IDE\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Jul  5  2025 Programmer\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 04:16 deps\n-rw-r--r--  1 nobody nogroup   76 Sep 28 04:15 gowin.tgz.sha256\ncat: /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
