every rvfi_* signal here is sized for a single\n        // channel, so the core's `_0` ports connect directly without\n        // slicing. No `_1` ports exist on the core's IO under nret=1.\n        .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid),\n        .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order),\n        .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn),\n        .io_rvfi_trap_0     (rvfi_trap),\n        .io_rvfi_halt_0     (rvfi_halt),\n        .io_rvfi_intr_0     (rvfi_intr),\n        .io_rvfi_mode_0     (rvfi_mode),\n        .io_rvfi_ixl_0      (rvfi_ixl),\n        .io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0 (rvfi_rs1_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0(rvfi_rs1_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0 (rvfi_rs2_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0(rvfi_rs2_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_rd_addr_0  (rvfi_rd_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0 (rvfi_rd_wdata),\n        .io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0 (rvfi_pc_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0 (rvfi_pc_wdata),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_addr_0 (rvfi_mem_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0(rvfi_mem_rmask),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0(rvfi_mem_wmask),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0(rvfi_mem_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0(rvfi_mem_wdata)\n    );\n\nendmodule\n29:- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r11s0 (regression, +1.87%): After operand collection absorbed PC and immediate selection and radix-4 trials shortened divider feedback, the path from `bypass_rs1_q` through the multiplier DSP to the registered low product limited median Fmax to 84.996 MHz.\n36:- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r13s1 (regression, +1.52%): Capturing fallback operands independently of the adjacent writer's alignment check moved the critical path to the EX/MEM bypass through rs1 and the integer ALU back to EX/MEM, limiting median Fmax to 93.627 MHz against a 96.48 MHz target.\n38:- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261121-001-r14s0 (regression, -0.64%): Predicting the carry or borrow into bit 16 from `B[15]` and repairing only adjacent dependents added 2,475 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, while the path from load predictor RAM through MEM t