{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_154","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check && diff -qr cores/bench/rtl \"$TMPDIR/rtl-routes\"; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Split shifts across EX and MEM\n\nEX shifts by the low three bits of the resolved RV32 distance. Collection predecodes SLLI, SRLI and SRAI at 8, 16 and 24 into fixed byte routes and disables their fine-shifter selects. The standalone ALU uses all five distance bits.\n\nEX/MEM holds the partial word, a completion flag, and one-hot left, right and sign-fill enables for the remaining byte displacement. MEM uses the registered routes to form the value shared by WB, operand collection and repair. A dependent successor waits one cycle and replaces each matching operand. An independent successor advances even when an immediate field aliases the producer's register. RVFI sources receive the exact value in that case. Load verification retains its separate early-hit check.\n\nVerilator lint and all six cocotb test runners passed. The local single-retirement formal suite passed all 53 checks on its first run for this implementation. Cosimulation passed all five ELFs. With both stall generators enabled, the ten CoreMark iterations took 3,044,495 cycles between markers 12,229 and 3,056,724. The UART reported all five canonical CRCs and the validation banner.\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 87.966, 92.972 and 92.972 MHz. The median corresponds to 305.38 CoreMark iterations per second and fell below the 101.74 MHz promotion threshold. On placement 1 the worst setup path ran from collected rs2 bit 0 through operand B, the carry chain and result selection to EX/MEM result bit 9.\n\nThe pipeline regression checks all 32 distances, positive and negative operands, each register forwarding age, adjacent dual-source latency, stalled load repair, stores, branches and division.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
