{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r11s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261121-001-r11s0\ntitle: Fold PC and immediate selection into the existing operand registers\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  EX currently selects the adjacent writer for each operand, then selects\n  PC or immediate for the integer ALU. Both selections sit ahead of the\n  arithmetic. In a scratch run, preparing ALU operands in collection\n  removed the second EX mux and matched all five CoreMark CRCs in\n  3,238,429 cycles. Keeping a separate pair of prepared operands cost\n  64 flip-flops and reached 83.470 MHz on Gowin placement 1, close to\n  the champion's 83.439 MHz. The opportunity is to share the existing\n  operand registers and the final bypass mux across EX consumers.\nhypothesis: |\n  Choose the values that EX will consume while the instruction is in\n  operand collection. Put PC in the first operand slot for AUIPC. Put\n  the immediate in the second slot for OP-IMM, LUI and AUIPC. Keep true\n  register operands for branches, multiplies, divides and store data.\n  The dedicated effective-address and JALR adders already take the\n  displacement separately. Decode the operand roles from validated\n  controls and qualify the adjacent bypass enables with those roles\n  at the collection edge. Each timed EX operand then has one two-input\n  mux shared by the units that use it.\n  \n  This should remove the cascaded operand muxes without duplicating the\n  wide collection-to-EX datapath. Keep full post-forward source values\n  for RVFI on a parallel trace-only path. The measurable target is a\n  median above 87.277 MHz at the champion's marker cycle count. The\n  remaining divider feedback and load-dependent redirect paths make\n  the size of the clock gain uncertain.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      In collection, select PC or immediate into the existing rs1_val and\n      rs2_val payloads after resolving eligible MEM and WB writers. Keep\n      rs2_val as the real store value for SB, SH and SW. Register role-gated\n      adjacent bypass bits on the same enable as the payload. Form the\n      load-to-branch comparison operand and RVFI snapshots from the real\n      collected values before substitution. Preserve reset, stalls and squash.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive the integer ALU from the two post-bypass operands directly.\n      The address and JALR adders continue using the separate immediate.\n      Use the original result enables for instructions that write an\n      ALU result. Reconstruct full trace operands using the trace snapshots,\n      original adjacent matches, fault qualification and formatted load\n      result, including operands held over a divide.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add raw source values and raw adjacent-match metadata for RVFI to\n      id_ex_t. Keep one pair of timing-visible collected data operands.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Initialize the added trace fields in the decode payload. Collection\n      fills them from the youngest eligible writers at transfer.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise an OP-IMM whose immediate bits name the preceding writer\n      and an AUIPC whose encoded rs1 bits name that writer. Check rd_wdata\n      and both raw RVFI operands. Follow an adjacent producer with a store\n      whose displacement and forwarded data differ, hold the bus unready,\n      and check the accepted address, byte lanes, write data and retirement.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
