d resolving trailing quotient-bit pairs with radix-4 trials across all three narrow lanes raised Fmax at the same CoreMark cycle count.\"}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261121-002-r12s1', 'title': 'Divide small divisors by table reciprocal and large divisors one octal digit per clock', 'category': 'structural', 'expected_impact': \"{'fitness_delta_pct': 7, 'confidence': 'medium'}\", 'changes': '[{\\'file\\': \\'rtl/alu.sv\\', \\'description\\': \"Implement the reciprocal ROM,\n…[2100 of 5172 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7672f8bec25b4bab]…\ns_baseline': '2355.2', 'fmax_mhz': '90.588', 'ipc_coremark': '3e-06', 'cycles': '3044309', 'iterations': '10', 'lut4': '4484', 'ff': '1848', 'seeds': '[87.454, 90.588, 90.588]', 'perturbations': '[[0, 87.454, 15], [1, 90.588, 13], [2, 90.588, 13]]', 'lutram': '8', 'bsram': '33', 'dsp': '6', 'critical_path': \"{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/residual_q_0_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/magnitude_q_31_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.435, 'arrival_ns': 16.729, 'logic_cells': 42, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\", 'logic_levels': '15', 'formal_passed': 'True', 'cosim_passed': 'True', 'error': 'None', 'implementation_notes': '', 'timestamp': '2026-11-21T21:58:21.878729Z', 'slot': '2', 'round_id': '12', 'lesson': '- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r12s2 (regression, +6.58%): Two multiply-subtract passes with conservative estimates from a 4,096-entry reciprocal ROM left a residual below twice the divisor, so one final conditional subtraction sufficed for every nonzero divisor and eliminated the restoring chains that limited Fmax.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
