{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261121-001-r13s0.last'","aggregated_output":"Wrote and schema-validated the [micro_opt hypothesis](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-001-r13s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r13s0.yaml). It registers adjacent operand matches one cycle earlier and interlocks a dependent consumer when alignment suppresses the producer’s write.\n\nThe prototype matched all five CoreMark CRCs in **3,044,309 cycles** and passed all 45 pipeline tests with the new fault latency. It needs a median Fmax above **96.473 MHz** to clear the acceptance margin. That timing gain remains unverified.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
