{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-00*-r7*.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-001-r7s0\ntitle: Pack replay words into one block RAM table and remove the BTB word mux\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion spent 179,329 of its 3,399,350 CoreMark marker cycles waiting\n  for an instruction while decode was free and EX was not redirecting.\n  Fetch selects among the external bus, a 32-bit word in each BTB entry,\n  and a separately tagged successor word. Storing the instruction once by\n  word PC removes a wide mux input and lets a trained word serve a wait\n  after any predecessor, including beyond the sixteenth sequential slot.\nhypothesis: |\n  Factor instruction storage out of the existing 64-entry BTB. Give\n  controls and ordinary instructions one 4,096-row synchronous replay RAM\n  indexed by PC[13:2]. Each 39-bit row holds the instruction, PC[19:14]\n  and a valid bit. Preserve the BTB indices, targets, two-bit direction\n  counters and EX training policy. The same EX write port can install\n  either kind of word. Read the held PC or the predicted next index on\n  the PC update edge. A redirect cancels that read. A ready external\n  word takes priority, including on recovery.\n\n  With separate BTB instruction words and ordinary-word RAM at this depth,\n  a scratch implementation took 3,245,848 cycles at 56.012 MHz on placement\n  1. Sharing the word RAM took 3,235,356 cycles. Gowin placements 0, 1\n  and 2 reached 56.111, 58.147 and 58.147 MHz, giving 179.72 iterations/s\n  at the median, 5.47% above 170.41. The ten-iteration run passed all five\n  CRCs under instruction and data stalls. At this cycle count the acceptance\n  threshold is 57.67 MHz. Selftest and all three random programs matched\n  the reference retirement trace with both stalls enabled. All 31 pipeline\n  cases passed in a scratch fixture that allowed the validity sweep to\n  finish before testing warm replay and checked the new fetch cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove the BTB word array and per-path successor slots.\n…[12554 of 15626 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:04cd4c67b14c381a]…\n or replay data in parallel with the tag\n      check. When a fetch miss or flush inserts a bubble, clear validity\n      and all effectful controls. Preserve ID/EX state on a backend hold.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Train and replay both sides of a conditional, a straight run beyond\n      sixteen words, and adjacent taken jumps. Check the warmed fetch rate,\n      exact RVFI PCs and words, order and store effects. Exercise an index\n      collision, an uninitialized word in a live group, retry on a held\n      collision, a JALR retarget after a stalled load, and FENCE.I with\n      replacement code. Check that a wrong-path store or divide annulled\n      in EX has no effects while the recovery word issues. Adapt cycle\n      expectations for the new allocation latency, longer runs and\n      recovery from either candidate. Preserve every architectural trace\n      and side-effect assertion, especially the replacement instruction\n      and register result in the short-loop collision test.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
