{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261121-001-r9s0.log'\nfor line in open(p):\n try: item=json.loads(line).get('item', {})\n except ValueError: continue\n if item.get('type')=='agent_message': print(item['text'][:1400])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"I’ll inspect the target checkout, implement the recovery and bubble changes, then run lint, formal, co-simulation, and timing.\nCoreMark matched the prototype’s 3,273,911 bracketed cycles with both buses stalling. All five CRCs and the validation banner passed. Selftest and all three random retirement traces also matched the ISS with and without stalls. Formal and the three Gowin placements are running.\nThe first implementation passed all 53 formal checks and all six cocotb suites. Its median was 71.917 MHz. The worst path now runs through the general ALU into data RAM, so I’ll test the separate effective-address register described in the hypothesis.\nSeparating address generation exposed the next critical path through load-to-branch comparison and redirect. Comparing the returned bytes directly in their RAM lanes brought placement 1 to 73.605 MHz. The stalled pipeline tests and ISS traces still pass. I’m checking whether registering the forwarding decision can close the remaining gap.\nPlacement 1 reached 76.093 MHz after MEM began reading the divide result from the existing lane registers. The duplicated result registers had become the critical endpoint. This version passed the arithmetic and pipeline tests. I’ll verify its three-placement median and rerun the full formal gate.\nThe final RTL passed all 53 formal checks. Gowin measured 77.828, 76.093, and 76.093 MHz across the three placements. The 76.093 MHz median clears the qualifying frequency by 1.294 MHz at the verified cycle count.\nA smaller version then reached 76.247 MHz on placement 1 with 35 fewer registers. It keeps the original decode flush and recovered-PC register. I’ll rerun all three placements and correctness checks on this version before selecting it.\n**76.247 MHz median**, 1.448 MHz above the qualifying threshold. CoreMark completed ten iterations in **3,273,911 bracketed cycles**, yielding **232.89 iterations/s**.\n\nLint, all 53 formal checks, all six cocotb suites, and co-simulation passed. All five CRCs and the validation banner matched.\n\n[Implementation notes covering replay recovery, address generation, load comparison, and divider result selection](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-001-r9s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
