{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r12s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-002-r12s1\ntitle: Divide small divisors by table reciprocal and large divisors one octal digit per clock\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion took 3,044,309 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations at 85.001 MHz.\n  Its reported placement-0 path crosses 59 cells from quotient to remainder in\n  divider lane 2, which performs three dependent 18-bit restores per clock.\n  CoreMark executes zero divides or remainders between its markers, so the\n  divider can raise the score by shortening the clock period. At that cycle\n  count the acceptance threshold is a median just above 88.91 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the five restoring lanes with two exact unsigned algorithms split\n  at divisor magnitude 2048. Capture magnitudes A and D on div_start. For\n  1 <= D < 2048, read M = floor((2^32 - 1)/D) from a synchronous 2048 by\n  32-bit constant ROM. A private registered-input multiplier computes\n  Q0 = high32(A*M), then P = Q0*D. The reciprocal is at most one unit below\n  2^32/D, so for 32-bit A the estimate is exact or one low. Round one reads\n  M. Round two registers A and M at the multiplier inputs, round three\n  captures Q0, and round four registers Q0 and D at the same inputs. Round\n  five captures the low word of P (P <= A) and Q0+1. Round six registers\n  A-P. On round seven, if A-P >= D, use Q0+1 and (A-P)-D. Otherwise use\n  Q0 and A-P. Register the requested magnitude on that edge.\n\n  For D >= 2048 the quotient fits in 21 bits. Seed the remainder with\n  A[31:21], and consume the remaining 21 bits in seven radix-8 digits.\n  For each digit form X = 8*R + next_three_bits. Compute X-k*D in parallel\n  for k=1 through 7, decode adjacent borrow flags into a one-hot digit, and\n  select the corresponding residual (X for digit zero). Keep X and the\n  multiples at 35 bits and retain a separate borrow. In round one X is only\n  A[31:18]. Compute its trials from the low 14 divisor bits with 17-bit\n  multiples and a borrow. Force digit zero when D[31:14] is nonzero.\n  In parallel register 3D, 5D and 7D from the captured D using shifts and\n  one add or subtract each. Shifts supply 2D, 4D and 6D for the remaining\n  six rounds. The 21-bit shift register that supplies the dividend bits\n  receives the three new quotient bits at each edge.\n\n  Transfer either result on the existing seventh edge, with the captured\n  operation, sign and divide-by-zero handling. The private multiplier\n  keeps divider operand switches off the ordinary EX low-MUL bypass.\n  A scratch implementation passed the divider and pipeline suites, exercised\n  every nonzero reciprocal entry, and matched the ISS on selftest and three\n  random programs under bus stalls. It passed the CoreMark CRC checks in\n  3,044,309 marker cycles. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 87.785,\n  91.086 and 91.086 MHz, giving 299.20 iterations/s (+7.16%). The median\n  placement's longest path ran from EX/MEM.alu_result to fetch read_mode.\n  The design used 5,079 logic cells, 2,063 registers, 29 BSRAMs and 5 DSPs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement the reciprocal ROM, registered product schedule, and radix-8\n      recurrence in the real divider. Initialize reciprocal[0] to zero and\n      generate rows 1..1023 and 1024..2047 in two constant loops to fit\n      Gowin's elaboration limit. Preserve div_start, div_last, div_accept,\n      held-result ownership, reset and the ALTOPS timing and formulas.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Extend the arithmetic oracle vectors with the 2047/2048 transition,\n      exact multiples and their neighbors, all eight first and final octal\n      digits, and wide divisors whose multiples exceed 32 bits. Exercise\n      consecutive requests crossing the split with sign changes and holds.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
