{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'ls -la cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/*r13s1* && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r13s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 3850 Nov 21 23:20 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r13s1.yaml\nid: hyp-20261121-002-r13s1\ntitle: Prepare execution operands and PC-relative results in collection\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's median Gowin placement traces EX/MEM result bit 0 through\n  address alignment and writer qualification to the next instruction's\n  32-bit operand register. A second path, only 0.004 ns shorter, goes\n  through the integer ALU into the EX/MEM result. At 3,044,309 cycles\n  for ten iterations, 96.48 MHz is sufficient to clear the 4.6% margin.\n  Eliminating every remaining bubble could gain only 4.19% at today's clock.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make the collection-to-EX register hold ready-to-use operands. Capture\n  each source from its youngest eligible MEM or WB writer, otherwise\n  from the saved register value, even when the immediate predecessor\n  matches. Register that predecessor's eligible match separately. EX\n  selects between the complete fallback and the single registered bypass.\n  Thus a late alignment check drives a one-bit\n  select flop without gating the 32-bit operand capture. Prepare the\n  ALU B fallback as a four-way masked OR of immediate, MEM, WB and saved\n  rs2. Folding the operand role into these source enables removes a mux\n  after forwarding. Capture AUIPC's existing direct-target sum, PC+4\n  for links, or the LUI immediate in a separate result register. EX can\n  then use rs1 directly as ALU A. Raw rs2 serves stores, branches and RVFI.\n  \n  The scratch prototype ran ten CoreMark iterations in 3,044,309 marker\n  cycles with both stalls enabled, all five CRCs and the validation banner.\n  All 45 pipeline tests passed. Selftest and the three random RVFI traces\n  matched the ISS with both stalls. In Gowin placement 1, selecting the\n  immediate after the forwarded rs2 mux reached 90.171 MHz. Folding the\n  immediate enable into the four parallel source terms reached 97.596 MHz.\n  Placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 87.381, 97.596 and 97.596 MHz. The median\n  gives 320.59 iterations/s, 5.82% above the champion.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      In each collected source value mask MEM, WB and waiting data by\n      fwd_sel == 1, 2 and 0 respectively. Keep repair and adjacent\n      qualification out of those masks. Beside id_ex_w, register ALU B\n      from four independently masked terms. The immediate enable is\n      waiting.ctrl.alu_src. Gate each rs2 source enable with !alu_src.\n      Capture the two raw adjacent selects and adjacent_rs2 && !alu_src\n      on !stall_ex. On that edge also register the OR of direct_target\n      masked by is_auipc, sequential_pc masked by is_jump and waiting.imm\n      masked by is_lui. Exclude those classes from the ordinary ALU\n      result enables. On repair && !mem_wait, write mem_wb_value directly\n      to each matched EX operand, including ALU B only for its own match,\n      and clear the bypass flags.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Select fwd_ex_mem or the corresponding complete fallback with a\n      two-input mux for rs1, rs2 and ALU B. Drive ALU A from rs1. In the\n      EX/MEM result OR replace the masked link term with the registered\n      collection result. Retain the low-product mux, speculative load\n      formatting, fault-qualified writer and separate rs1 + imm address\n      path. Hold all of these inputs across downstream backpressure.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Test AUIPC at PC 0x1ffc with immediate 0xfffff000 and consume the\n      expected 0x00000ffc on the next instruction. Follow a stalled load\n      with an ADDI whose immediate bits alias the load destination in\n      the raw rs2 field. Check both the corrected RVFI rs2 snapshot and\n      the immediate-based sum. Retain the existing faulting JALR and\n      adjacent faulting load tests for writer eligibility.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
