{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261121-002-r2s1.last cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r2s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"Wrote and schema-validated [hyp-20261121-002-r2s1.yaml](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-002-r2s1-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r2s1.yaml).\n\nThe hypothesis splits the divider by divisor magnitude, shortening its critical path while preserving six-round latency. A scratch prototype reached **47.203 MHz median** and validated all five CoreMark CRCs in **4,491,485 marker cycles**. That yields **105.09 iterations/s**, a **7.61% gain** over the champion, above the 4.6% acceptance margin. The tournament implementation still needs its official evaluation.id: hyp-20261121-002-r2s1\ntitle: Split the six-round divider by divisor magnitude\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Gowin traced the champion's 197-cell setup path from quotient_q[35] to\n  remainder_q[12] through six dependent 33-bit restoring steps. This limits\n  all instructions to a median 43.865 MHz, even though CoreMark retired zero\n  divides or remainders in its 4,491,485 marker cycles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use two unsigned restoring datapaths under the existing six-round controller.\n  Let A and D be the 32-bit operand magnitudes. For 0 < D < 2^14, every\n  restored remainder fits in 14 bits. This lane can consume six dividend bits\n  per clock with 15-bit trial subtractors. For D >= 2^14, the top 14 bits of A\n  already form a valid remainder smaller than D. Seed the wide lane with that\n  prefix and consume the remaining 18 bits in six groups of three. Only three\n  33-bit subtractors lie in series on this lane. Both lanes advance together.\n  One bit captured at issue selects the result after the final round.\n\n  A scratch prototype reached 43.834, 47.203 and 47.203 MHz on Gowin placement\n  options 0, 1 and 2. It used 2,839 LUT4s against the champion's 2,756.\n  CoreMark validated all five CRCs in 4,491,485 marker cycles with both bus\n  stalls enabled. The median gives 105.09 iterations/s, 7.61% above 97.66.\n  The reported option-0 worst path moved to the register-file, EX redirect\n  and ID hazard logic. The implementation needs a median above 45.882 MHz\n  at this cycle count to clear the acceptance margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Share the registered divisor magnitude, sign flags and round counter.\n      Initialize the narrow lane's 36-bit quotient shift register to four\n      zero bits followed by A and its 14-bit remainder to zero. Append six\n      quotient bits per round. Initialize the wide lane's 18-bit quotient\n      shift register to A[17:0] and its 32-bit remainder to zero-extended\n      A[31:18]. Append three quotient bits per round. In both lanes take\n      dividend bits MSB first. Keep digit calculation local to each lane.\n      For D=0 select the wide lane. Subtraction by zero emits 18 ones and\n      reconstructs A in the remainder. Fill the upper 14 quotient bits\n      with the captured zero-divisor flag. Apply the existing RV32M sign\n      correction after selecting the magnitude. Preserve the six-round\n      handshake, held result, reset and all ALTOPS equations.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Extend the integer-reference checks for all four operations with divisor\n      magnitudes 0x3fff, 0x4000 and 0x4001, including negative signed operands.\n      At D=0x4000 check A=0xffffffff, which sets all 18 wide quotient bits and\n      leaves remainder 0x3fff. Alternate lanes on consecutive requests and\n      include zero divisors, INT_MIN/-1 and held results. Keep the existing\n      exact completion-cycle and pipeline forwarding checks.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
