{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -1 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r14s1\", \"title\": \"Capture the adjacent producer directly in each consumer operand register\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion runs ten iterations in 3,044,309 cycles at 97.260 MHz.\\nIts placement-0 worst path starts at EX/MEM result bit 2 and ends at\\ndecode valid. In placement 1, the path through the integer ALU and\\nthe path from a source register to fetch recovery are 0.001 ns apart.\\nBoth use EX operands assembled from a saved value and a shared\\n32-bit feedback bus. The round-13 collection experiment still put\\nthis last source selection in front of the consumer's ALU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion runs ten iterations in 3,044,309 cycles at 97.260 MHz.\\nIts placement-0 worst path starts at EX/MEM result bit 2 and ends at\\ndecode valid. In placement 1, the path through the integer ALU and\\nthe path from a source register to fetch recovery are 0.001 ns apart.\\nBoth use EX operands assembled from a saved value and a shared\\n32-bit feedback bus. The round-13 collection experiment still put\\nthis last source selection in front of the consumer's ALU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move delivery of the immediately preceding result to the edge on which\\nthe consumer enters EX. Give each source register its own result\\nselection. In parallel with producer execution, collection determines\\nwhether that port takes the adjacent writer or its existing MEM, WB\\nor saved-register fallback. An adjacent match enables the producer's\\nselected integer function, link PC, low product or formatted load.\\nFor integer functions, combine each source match with the producer's\\none-hot result_sel bits while the adder, shifter and logic functions\\nare working. Feed the masked function outputs, link, product, load\\nand saved fallback into that port's result tree. The arithmetic units\\nare shared. Only the two destination selection trees are separate.\\nBoth source ports can capture the same producer on one edge. EX can\\nstart a dependent branch comparison, address sum or multiply directl\n…[4115 of 7187 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d58f7b7552d9d028]…\ness\": 253.86, \"delta_pct\": -20.54, \"vs_baseline\": 1994.55, \"fmax_mhz\": 77.284, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3044309, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4770, \"ff\": 1931, \"seeds\": [66.762, 77.284, 77.284], \"perturbations\": [[0, 66.762, 10], [1, 77.284, 10], [2, 77.284, 10]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 25, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/id_ex_w.rs1_val_31_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/id_ex_w.rs1_val_2_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.979, \"arrival_ns\": 20.273, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_mul\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T23:55:45.276759Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261121-002-r14s1 (regression, -20.54%): Capturing an adjacent MUL's low 32 bits directly in each consumer operand register put the multiplier DSP and per-port result mux on the same EX feedback path, cutting median Fmax from 97.260 to 77.284 MHz at the same CoreMark cycle count.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
