{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 5 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Shorten the champion's divider feedback path with radix-4 digits\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"On the current BTB-equipped core, Gowin traced a 28.668 ns path from\\nremainder_q to quotient_q through six dependent restoring steps. That\\npath limits the clock on all 4,043,251 CoreMark marker cycles. The\\nearlier radix-4 experiment reached 47.652 MHz on the pre-BTB core.\\nAt the champion's cycle count, a median above 45.40 MHz would clear\\nthe 4.6% acceptance margin.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"On the current BTB-equipped core, Gowin traced a 28.668 ns path from\\nremainder_q to quotient_q through six dependent restoring steps. That\\npath limits the clock on all 4,043,251 CoreMark marker cycles. The\\nearlier radix-4 experiment reached 47.652 MHz on the pre-BTB core.\\nAt the champion's cycle count, a median above 45.40 MHz would clear\\nthe 4.6% acceptance margin.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Compute two quotient bits at a time inside the existing six-round\\ndivider. For each digit, form X = 4*R + the next two dividend bits.\\nSubtract D, 2D and 3D from X in parallel. The largest multiple that\\nfits gives the digit and its difference gives the next remainder.\\nThis cuts the serial remainder selections per full round from six\\nto three, while preserving the divide handshake and every instruction's\\nissue timing.\\n\\nA scratch prototype on the current core reached 44.708, 47.393 and\\n47.393 MHz on Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2. In each placement\\nthe worst path started at the register file. Option 0 used 3,297 LUT4s,\\nup from 2,985. With both bus stalls enabled, CoreMark validated all\\nfive CRCs in 4,043,251 marker cycles for ten iterations. The median\\ngives 117.22 iterations/s, 9.2% above the 107.34 champion.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture unsigned operand magnitudes at issue. In round one resolve\\nthe top two dividend bits with a small comparison against D=0,1,2,3\\no\n…[34616 of 37688 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:54e258965a68bb0a]…\n 139.52, \"delta_pct\": 14.01, \"vs_baseline\": 1051.16, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.506, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3548404, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3648, \"ff\": 953, \"seeds\": [49.085, 49.506, 49.506], \"perturbations\": [[0, 49.085, 20], [1, 49.506, 21], [2, 49.506, 21]], \"lutram\": 24, \"bsram\": 14, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/read_valid_q_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -15.373, \"arrival_ns\": 25.667, \"logic_cells\": 33, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 20, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T14:53:47.283889Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r4s1 (improvement, +14.01%): Finishing the last two quotient bits and all multiplies in MEM shortened divider feedback and removed the multiply DSP from the EX address path, at the cost of one load-use bubble when the next instruction needs the result from MEM/WB.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
