{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r9s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-003-r9s2\ntitle: Predict load words during operand collection for forwarding in EX\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion executes 544,852 loads in 3,273,911 marker cycles. Its\n  adjacent LW-to-pointer and load-to-branch paths both consume live MEM\n  data in EX. Round eight's predicted-index word replay saved 145,087\n  cycles on its parent, but still sent the MEM response through those\n  bypasses. The champion's operand-collection stage offers a full extra\n  cycle to look up a load before either consumer needs its value.\nhypothesis: |\n  Start a synchronous, PC-assisted word lookup as a load leaves operand\n  collection. Predict the base from an available producer or the saved register value.\n  For consecutive pointer loads, use the preceding lookup's raw word\n  directly as the candidate base. Form the low six address bits by addition.\n  Predict word-index bits [12:6] by XORing the candidate base with the\n  change observed at the last execution of the same instruction. The\n  instruction replay row already has seven spare successor bits on a\n  sequential instruction. Its low eleven successor bits still steer fetch.\n\n  In EX, compare the guessed base with the fully forwarded base in four\n  independent byte slices. In parallel, add the displacement to the saved\n  guess and compare its word index, high address tag and RAM range with\n  the returned row. Register these comparisons, alignment and store\n  collision checks alongside the raw word and its formatted load value.\n  Register the preceding producer's write permission with each source\n  match. The following EX stage can use one registered forwarding value\n  while MEM combines the checks. A verified hit completes the load\n  internally. On a miss, MEM requests the exact external address. An\n  independent younger instruction proceeds when that transaction completes.\n  A dependent instruction holds in EX, captures the accepted operand and\n  executes on the following cycle. This takes live data RAM off the\n  immediate load-to-branch and load-to\n…[3412 of 6484 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d6c8526cba3046a6]…\nction while MEM\n      verifies it. Gate redirect, divide start, predictor training and the\n      EX/MEM transfer on successful validation or completed operand repair.\n      Preserve the raw word, exact address, byte masks and single retirement\n      for RVFI. Use the registered candidate in the consumer datapath\n      independently of the tag comparison. On a miss, suppress all of that\n      consumer's effects until MEM supplies its correct operand. Hold the\n      forwarding register with EX/MEM under backpressure.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Include the predictor in the pipeline test's RTL source list. Compare\n      cold and warmed pointer chains, load-dependent branches and subword\n      ALU consumers. Force a wrong mask, a same-index different tag, stores\n      on each lookup edge, a partial store and a stalled bus miss. Check the\n      retry issues no duplicate transaction or retirement, wrong-path stores\n      stay squashed, and a faulting load preserves the previous writer.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
