{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\ncycles=3044309\nprint('fitness',10*92.638e6/cycles)\nprint('gain',(10*92.638e6/cycles/279.21-1)*100)\nPY\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r12s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"fitness 304.2989394309185\ngain 8.985687987865232\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r12s0\ntitle: Resolve trailing quotient-bit pairs in the three narrow divider lanes\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Gowin traced the champion's placement-0 setup path from quotient_q[20]\n  to remainder_q[0] in divider lane 2. The 16.781 ns path crosses 59 cells.\n  That lane chains three 18-bit restoring decisions per clock. Pairing its\n  first two trials in a scratch build raised median Fmax from 85.001 to\n  87.266 MHz and moved the limiting path to lane 0, where five dependent\n  trials remain. CoreMark took 3,044,309 marker cycles in both designs.\n  At that cycle count the acceptance threshold is about 88.91 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Resolve the trailing quotient-bit pairs of lanes 0, 1 and 2 with\n  radix-4 restoring trials. In each round, consume bits from the MSB\n  in groups of (1,2,2) for the 4-bit lane, (2,2) for the 11-bit lane,\n  and (1,2) for the 18-bit lane. Each pair computes three candidate\n  differences concurrently. A balanced two-level mux selects the restored\n  remainder. This cuts the dependent selections from five to three in\n  lane 0 and from three to two in lanes 1 and 2. Lane 3 uses its two\n  binary trials and lane 4 uses one. A shared 20-bit triple of the low\n  18 divisor-magnitude bits suffices for all three paired lanes.\n  A scratch build reached 92.638 MHz on Gowin placement 1.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      On div_start register 3*divisor_abs[17:0] in 20 bits using a\n      widened shift and add. For each radix-4 pair in a W-bit lane, form\n      X = {R,next_two_bits} and subtract D, 2D and the low W+2 bits of\n      registered 3D in parallel. Zero-extend before subtracting in W+3\n      bits. The top bit of each difference gives lt1, lt2 or lt3. Use\n      lt2 to select between (lt1 ? X : X-D) and (lt3 ? X-2D : X-3D),\n      retaining the low W bits. Append {!lt2, !lt3 || (lt2 && !lt1)}\n      to the quotient. Preserve each lane's prefix seed, seven-round\n      schedule, result hold, signed correction, divide-by-zero handling\n      and formal ALTOPS path.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
