{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nxs=[json.loads(l) for l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor v in xs[-6:]:\n print(v['id'],v['seeds'],v['critical_path']); print(v['hypothesis']['hypothesis']); print(v['implementation_notes'][:3000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r11s0 [78.389, 84.996, 84.996] {'from': 'cpu/id_ex_w.rs1_val_4_s0', 'to': 'cpu/id_ex_w.valid_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.757, 'arrival_ns': 18.051, 'logic_cells': 36, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu']}\nChoose the values that EX will consume while the instruction is in\noperand collection. Put PC in the first operand slot for AUIPC. Put\nthe immediate in the second slot for OP-IMM, LUI and AUIPC. Keep true\nregister operands for branches, multiplies, divides and store data.\nThe dedicated effective-address and JALR adders already take the\ndisplacement separately. Decode the operand roles from validated\ncontrols and qualify the adjacent bypass enables with those roles\nat the collection edge. Each timed EX operand then has one two-input\nmux shared by the units that use it.\n\nThis should remove the cascaded operand muxes without duplicating the\nwide collection-to-EX datapath. Keep full post-forward source values\nfor RVFI on a parallel trace-only path. The measurable target is a\nmedian above 87.277 MHz at the champion's marker cycle count. The\nremaining divider feedback and load-dependent redirect paths make\nthe size of the clock gain uncertain.\n\n\nhyp-20261121-002-r11s1 [86.229, 86.95, 86.95] {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_6_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/read_mode_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.597, 'arrival_ns': 16.891, 'logic_cells': 17, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_if']}\nReplace all five restoring lanes with a synchronous reciprocal ROM, a\nsmall interpolation multiply, and two uses of the existing EX multiplier.\nCapture unsigned magnitudes A and D and the architectural sign and zero\nflags on issue. For nonzero D let k = floor(log2(D)) and N = D << (31-k).\nRound one reads ROM row i = N[30:21] and registers t = N[20:8] and k.\nFor j from 0 through 1024 define U(j) = ceil(2^42/(1024+j)). Store\nU(i)-1 in 32 bits and floor((U(i)-U(i+1))/32) in 17 bits. Generate these\ncoefficients from integer constants at elaboration. Round two multiplies\nthe slope by t. Round three subtracts the product shifted \n…[9111 of 12183 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a35e652a654e4c38]…\n. Let\ne = 1-D*M/H. Each pass leaves a residual below D+e*R. For D<H/2,\nthe maximum of e+H*e^2/D is below 0.668 over the ROM buckets.\nWithin each bucket M is constant and that expression decreases with\nD. Checking its smallest divisor covers all 43,007 nonempty buckets\nbelow H/2. This gives a second residual below 2D. For D >= H/2 the\ntrue unsigned quotient is at most one, so one correction also suffices.\n\nA scratch RTL prototype passed the existing ALU, multiplier and\npipeline suites. A separate Verilator driver checked 1,001,100\nseven-round divide and remainder results against integer arithmetic.\nSelftest and all three random programs matched the reference\nretirements with both stall generators. CoreMark took 3,044,309\nmarker cycles and produced all five expected CRCs and the validation\nbanner under the same stalls.\nGowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 88.617, 91.713 and 91.713 MHz.\nTheir median gives 301.26 iterations/s, 7.90% above 279.21. The\noption-0 report used 4,587 logic cells, 33 BSRAMs and 6 DSPs.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
