{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r10s0','r8s1')): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\ndate -u\"","aggregated_output":"Insert an operand-collection stage between decode and EX. Capture the\nnewest available value for each source from MEM, WB or the decoded\nregister-file value, in that order. Register the tag match against the\ninstruction currently in EX. In the following cycle EX needs just one\nlate bypass, from its immediate predecessor. Preserve the specialized\nload-to-equality-branch and LW-to-pointer-load paths. A redirect kills\nboth younger slots. A dependency bubble holds the waiting consumer.\n\nThe new MEM-to-operand path makes the divider finish part of this\nstage boundary. With the existing two serial tail subtractions in MEM,\nthe prototype reached 55.975 MHz on placement 1, limited by a path\nfrom the divisor register to a collected operand. Use the existing\nEX-to-MEM transfer edge for a seventh restoring round. Register the\nfull quotient and remainder there so MEM only selects the magnitude\nand applies the sign or divide-by-zero result before forwarding it.\nThis preserves the eight-cycle spacing of independent divides.\n\nThe retimed prototype completed ten iterations in 3,273,911 bracketed\ncycles with both stalls and all five canonical CRCs. The extra recovery\nslot costs 50,011 cycles versus the champion. Gowin placement options\n0, 1 and 2 reached 60.455, 66.399 and 66.399 MHz. The median yields\n202.81 iterations/s, 7.64 percent above 188.41. The acceptance floor\nat this cycle count is 64.522 MHz to the nearest qualifying kHz.\nPlacement 0 used 4,116 LUT4s, 1,476 registers, 15 BSRAMs and two DSPs.\nAll 53 ALTOPS formal checks passed. Selftest and all three random\nprograms matched the reference traces with and without stalls.\n\nAll 34 pipeline cases passed in a scratch suite after rephasing\n13 timing-sensitive cases for the added slot. Adding one NOP before\nthe body-fill test's backedge aligned the same-row lookup with its\nfill again. The test checked the exact retry sequence and both\nretirements of the replacement instruction. The ALU suite also\npassed with vectors on both sides of all four new lane boundaries\nand an explicit seventh-edge transfer test.\n\nMove the existing DSP multiply to EX. Give the low product a dedicated\nenable in the ordinary EX result mux so the next instruction can use\nit through the existing bypass. Capture the high product separately at\nEX/MEM and select it in MEM for MULH, MULHU and MULHSU. This removes the\nlive DSP output from operand collection and saves the dependency bubble\non MUL. Decode the result enables in collection so adding the low product\ncosts one input to the EX result reduction. In paired placement-1 trials\nthe cascaded ALU/link/product mux reached 79.211 MHz. Forming the eleven\nmasked integer terms inside the ALU, then ORing its output with the enabled\nPC+4 and low product in EX reached 83.677 MHz.\n\nThe scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,238,429 bracketed\ncycles with both bus stalls, saving 35,482 cycles. All five CRCs and the\nvalidation banner matched. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 79.634,\n83.677 and 83.677 MHz. The 83.677 MHz median gives 258.39 iterations/s,\n7.99% above 239.26. The qualifying median is 81.047 MHz.\nPlacement 0 used 3,892 LUT4s, 1,413 registers and two DSPs.\nAll 53 ALTOPS formal checks and all six cocotb suites passed. Selftest\nand the three random programs matched the reference with and without stalls.\n\nSat Nov 21 22:07:52 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
