{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('003-r3s2'):\n  print(d['hypothesis'])\nprint(122.37*1.046*3511720/1e7)\nPY\nrg -n 'cosim-build|CXX|elf|CROSS' Makefile && ls /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh && ls bench/programs && rg -n 'MARKER|cycles|coremark|usage' test/cosim/main.cpp | tail -60\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': 'The champion took 4,043,251 marker cycles. Replaying the branch instruction\\non a branch target buffer (BTB) hit saved 154,266 cycles in the previous experiment.\\nThe BTB predicts where execution continues, but fetch still waits for imem\\non the ordinary instructions along that path. Repeated loop backedges and\\ncalls give the predictor several consecutive fetches it can anticipate.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Give each BTB index two successor sequences, one per branch outcome. At a\\nBTB hit, the predicted direction selects the sequence. Read its first word\\non the same clock edge that installs the predicted next PC. As fetch advances,\\npredict successive words along that path, up to 16 ordinary instructions.\\nAn EX correction selects the sequence for the actual outcome. Each saved\\nword carries its own PC tag. Checking it against the current fetch PC rejects\\na stale sequence when a JALR changes target or two branches share an index.\\nThe ready external response has first priority, then the BTB branch word,\\nthen the predicted successor word.\\n\\nA scratch RTL prototype completed ten canonical CoreMark iterations in\\n3,511,720 marker cycles with all five CRCs, 13.15% fewer cycles than the\\nchampion. Sharing one 16-word sequence between the two directions cost\\n39,471 extra cycles. Separate sequences reached 41.280, 42.159 and\\n42.159 MHz across the three Gowin placement options. The median gives\\n120.05 iterations/s, 11.84% above 107.34. At this cycle count the\\nimplementation must exceed 39.429 MHz to clear the acceptance margin.\\nPlacement option zero used 3,529 LUT4s and 14 BSRAMs. Its worst path ran\\nfrom the register file through EX to the successor read-valid register.\\nThe prototype passed 53 single-retirement formal checks and 92 cocotb\\ncases, including four directed replay cases. Selftest and the three random\\nprograms matched the reference retirement trace with both stall generators on.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 12, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.s\n…[2741 of 5813 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ecfaaadf41e2084e]…\n\t$(MAKE) -f bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/selftest.elf\n137:fpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\n143:bench/programs/coremark.elf: bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/crt0.S \\\n148:\t$(MAKE) -f bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/coremark.elf\n180:\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\n/opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh\nMakefile\ncoremark\ncrt0.S\ngen_random_trace.py\nlink.ld\nrandom1.S\nrandom2.S\nrandom3.S\nselftest.S\n35:// bench_cycles = stop - start, excluding init/CRC-printing overhead.\n63:        std::cerr << \"usage: sim <elf> [maxcycles] [--bench] [--istall] [--dstall] [--seed N]\\n\";\n66:    uint64_t maxcycles = argc > 2 ? atoll(argv[2]) : 50000000ULL;\n70:    //           (tools/eval/fpga.py:run_coremark_ipc) passes BOTH so the\n113:    for(uint64_t cycle=0; cycle<maxcycles; cycle++) {\n255:        // benchmark hit maxcycles without completing and the reading is invalid.\n267:        printf(\"{\\\"ebreak\\\":%s,\\\"maxcycles_hit\\\":%s,\\\"oob\\\":%s,\"\n279:    // Non-zero exit if sim ran out of cycles OR an out-of-bounds memory\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
