{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r4s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261121-001-r4s0\ntitle: Narrow the divider feedback path using the divisor magnitude\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion clocks at 42.974 MHz. Gowin traced its 170-cell worst path\n  from remainder_q[1] to remainder_q[13] through six serial restoring steps.\n  CoreMark executes zero divide or remainder instructions in its 3,511,720\n  marker cycles, so every clock saved here benefits other instructions.\n  At that cycle count the required median to clear the acceptance margin is\n  44.950 MHz. A prior magnitude split reached 46.056 MHz on the pre-BTB core.\nhypothesis: |\n  Select the precision of the six-round divider from the unsigned divisor\n  magnitude D. If 0 < D < 2\"'^14, the partial remainder always fits 14 bits.\n  This permits six 15-bit trial subtractions per round. For D >= 2''^14, the\n  top 14 bits of the dividend A are already smaller than D. Seed the\n  remainder with those bits and consume the other 18 bits in three full-width\n  trials per round. Each divider path then has either narrow trials or a\n  shorter chain. Both finish on the existing sixth round.\n  \n  A scratch build on the current path-replay core reached 43.681, 46.410\n  and 46.410 MHz across the three Gowin placements. Option zero used 3,585\n  LUT4s and its worst path started at the register file. At the champion'\"'s\n  marker count the median projects to 132.16 iterations/s, an 8.0% gain.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture the mode with the existing sign flags at issue. Initialize\n      the narrow lane with four zero bits followed by A in its 36-bit\n      quotient register and a zero 14-bit remainder. Initialize the wide\n      lane with A[17:0] in an 18-bit quotient register and zero-extended\n      A[31:18] in a 32-bit remainder. Both lanes shift dividend bits MSB\n      first. Select the retiring lane's quotient or remainder before the\n      existing sign correction. Route D=0 to the wide lane, whose 18\n      successful trials reconstruct A in the remainder. Fill the upper\n      14 quotient bits with the zero-divisor flag. Preserve reset,\n      completion backpressure, all ALTOPS equations and six-round timing.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Use the existing integer oracle and six-round handshake checks at\n      divisor magnitudes 0x3fff, 0x4000 and 0x4001, including negative\n      operands for DIV and REM. Check 0xffffffff divided by 0x4000\n      produces quotient 0x3ffff and remainder 0x3fff. Alternate modes\n      on consecutive requests, including zero divisors and held results.\n'''.replace('  \\\\n','\\\\n'))\nPY\ngit check-ignore -v cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r4s0.yaml && python - <<'PY'\nprint(46.410e7/3511720)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
