ssue capture the magnitudes and sign flags. In narrow mode start\n      R at zero and Q at {4'\"'b0,A}. In wide mode, including D=0, start R at\n      zero-extended A[31:18]. For group g from 0 through 5, initialize\n      Q[6*g +: 6] to {3'b000,A[3*g +: 3]}.\n\n      Feed the narrow recurrence with R[13:0] and Q[35:30], and the wide\n      recurrence with R[31:0] and Q[32:30]. Each step appends one input bit\n      MSB first, subtracts D at its trial width and restores on borrow.\n      Use the captured mode to write the selected residual to R. Shift Q\n      left by six and insert either six narrow quotient bits or three zeros\n      followed by the three wide bits. After six rounds the narrow quotient\n      is Q[31:0]. Gather the low three bits of each six-bit group in order\n      for the wide quotient. Fill its upper 14 bits with copies of D==0.\n      For D=0 the wide residual reconstructs A and every quotient bit is one.\n      Apply the existing result selection and sign correction. Retain reset,\n      done/accept behavior, INT_MIN/-1 semantics and all ALTOPS equations.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Check DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU against the integer oracle on both\n      sides of D=0x4000, including negative signed operands and transitions\n      through D=0. At D=0x4000 use dividends q*D+r with a different octal\n      digit in each of the six quotient groups. Exercise each group alone\n      and r in {0,1,D-1} to catch reversed groups, dropped bits and borrow\n      errors. Retain the exact six-round deadline and held-result checks.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r4s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.Draft7Validator(json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'))).validate(d)\nassert d['id']==p.stem and d['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert all((Path('cores/bench')/c['file']).is_file() for c in d['changes']