{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat 'cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r5s0.yaml'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261121-001-r5s0\ntitle: Register redirect recovery before addressing successor replay RAM\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On the 49.506 MHz champion, Gowin traced a 25.667 ns setup path from the\n  register file through EX to read_valid_q in fetch. A forwarded branch or\n  JALR operand can determine the recovery path and slot, which then select\n  replay metadata and enter the RAM collision check on the same edge.\n  Correcting the fetch PC needs the resolved target immediately. Reading\n  the successor RAM for that target can wait one edge.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing EX-to-PC redirect and decode flush. Launch successor\n  reads using the predicted path, sequential slot and fetch hold signals.\n  On a redirect, register the recovery event, the resolved branch path and\n  its replay eligibility. Mask the speculative RAM response on the next\n  cycle. The corrected PC can still fetch immediately from imem or the BTB.\n  If that fetch holds, request recovery slot zero. If it accepts an ordinary\n  word, request recovery slot one. An accepted BTB control starts its own\n  predicted path. This cuts the same-cycle EX redirect out of the replay\n  address, path-valid lookup, slot-limit lookup and collision comparison.\n  The potential IPC cost is one extra wait for a redirected first word\n  obtainable only from successor RAM. Check bracketed cycles and median\n  Gowin Fmax together against the 145.94 iterations/s acceptance threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive the successor RAM and its parallel metadata reads from fetch\n      state and registered recovery information. Give reset and FENCE.I\n      invalidation priority, and suppress the outstanding speculative\n      response on every redirect, including an ineligible recovery path.\n      Keep replay training, per-word PC tag checks, initialization bounds\n      and same-edge read/write collision suppression. A held corrected PC\n      retries the same slot until decode accepts it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
