-r3s0 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -16.628, 'arrival_ns': 26.923, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} \nhyp-20261121-002-r3s1 {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_12_s0', 'slack_ns': -18.031, 'arrival_ns': 28.325, 'logic_cells': 185, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu\n…[3815 of 6887 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7e8b6606b4177c11]…\nrom these registers.\n\nA scratch prototype reached 51.143, 54.790 and 54.790 MHz on Gowin\nplacements 0, 1 and 2. With the lane selection on the input to the MEM\ntail, the same three-lane design reached 53.100 MHz median. Registering\nthe merge on round six lifted the median to 54.790 MHz and moved its\nworst path to fetch replay control. The prototype used 4,054 LUT4s and\n1,109 FFs against the champion's 3,824 and 953. Ten CoreMark iterations\npassed all five CRCs in 3,399,350 marker cycles with both stall generators\nenabled. That gives 161.18 iterations/s, 6.58% above 151.23. At this\ncycle count the acceptance threshold is 53.7732 MHz. The prototype passed\nall 53 ALTOPS formal checks and 98 cocotb cases. Selftest and all three\nrandom programs matched the reference retirement trace under bus stalls.\n\nhyp-20261121-003-r6s2 {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_29_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_4_s0', 'slack_ns': -15.474, 'arrival_ns': 25.768, 'logic_cells': 144, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']} \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
