{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor x in map(json.loads, open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if x.get('round_id',0) in (4,5,7):\n  print(x['id'],x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r4s0 Capture one mode bit from the unsigned divisor magnitude D. For\n0 < D < 2^14, every restored remainder fits in 14 bits, so all six\ntrials per clock need only 15 bits each. For D >= 2^14, the top 14 bits\nof the dividend magnitude A are already smaller than D. Seed the remainder\nwith that prefix and resolve the remaining 18 bits in three full-width\ntrials per clock. Pack those 18 bits into six groups in the same 36-bit\nshift register. One pair of state registers then serves both precisions\nwith the original six-round latency.\n\nA scratch prototype on the current core reached 45.815, 46.666 and\n46.666 MHz on Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2. Option zero used\n3,640 LUT4s and 827 registers, up 85 LUT4s and one register. Its worst\npath moved from divider feedback to the register file through EX to dmem.\nWith both bus stalls enabled, ten CoreMark iterations completed in\n3,511,720 marker cycles with all five canonical CRCs. The median gives\n132.89 iterations/s, 8.59% above 122.37. The acceptance threshold at\nthat cycle count is 44.950 MHz. The prototype also passed 28 ALU and\n24 pipeline cocotb cases, including the new quotient-packing checks.\n\nhyp-20261121-002-r4s1 Make MEM/WB the first bypass point for every M-extension result.\nMultiply the operands already captured in EX/MEM during MEM. For division,\nuse the existing six clocks in EX to consume the top 30 dividend bits,\nfive per clock. Carry the instruction across EX/MEM and use its MEM clock\nfor the last two quotient bits and sign correction. An independent\ninstruction can issue immediately after a multiply. An adjacent consumer\nof any M result uses the existing load-use bubble and MEM/WB bypass.\nThis schedules the work around one common result boundary and keeps the\nmultiply DSP and final divider selection off the EX address path.\n\nA scratch prototype ran ten CoreMark iterations in 3,548,404 bracketed\ncycles with both bus stalls and all five CRCs validated. The extra\n36,684 cycles are a 1.04% cost. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached\n44.792, 4\n…[9373 of 12445 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b52a145d2b19e48a]…\nx modulo 2,048. Store the remaining\nseven tag bits from the actual destination, including the carry across\nan 8 KiB boundary. The taken bank needs the full destination word tag.\n\nA scratch prototype using 2,048 fall-through rows and 512 taken rows\ncompleted ten iterations in 3,207,645 marker cycles with both bus stall\ngenerators and all five CRCs correct. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2\nreached 54.800, 59.009 and 59.009 MHz. The median yields 183.96 iter/s,\n7.95 percent above the champion. A paired build storing all eleven low\nbits took exactly the same cycles and reached 57.114 MHz median. The\ncompact layout used 17 BSRAMs across the timed design. Placement remains\na risk since the acceptance threshold at this cycle count is 57.176 MHz.\nSelftest and all three stalled random traces matched the reference.\nFive existing pipeline cases stopped at fetch-visit assertions, including\nthe replacement-word collision case. Implementation must verify the\nresulting retirements and newest trained word under those schedules.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom shutil import copytree\nimport os\nw=Path(os.environ['TMPDIR'])/'r8micro'\ncopytree('bench/programs',w/'bench/programs')\n(w/'sim.sh').write_text('''set -e\nd=\\\"\"'$TMPDIR/r8micro\"\nRTL_DIR=\"$d/$1\" OBJ_DIR=\"$d/$1-obj\" NRET=1 bash test/cosim/build.sh > \"$d/$1-verilator.log\" 2>&1\n\"$d/$1-obj/cosim_sim\" \"$d/bench/programs/coremark.elf\" 50000000 --bench --istall --dstall | tee \"$d/$1-coremark.json\"\n'\"''')\ndef early(r):\n p = r/'core.sv'\n s=p.read_text()\n start = s.index('  forward_unit u_fwd')\n end = s.index('  // ── RVFI',start)\n s=s[:start]+'''  logic [1:0] match_mem, match_wb;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (\"'!stall_id) begin\n      match_mem[0] <= id_ex_w.rd != 0 && id_ex_w.rd == if_id_w.instr[19:15];\n      match_mem[1] <= id_ex_w.rd != 0 && id_ex_w.rd == if_id_w.instr[24:20];\n      match_wb[0] <= ex_mem_w.rd != 0 && ex_mem_w.rd == if_id_w.instr[19:15];\n      match_wb[1] <= ex_mem_w.rd != 0 && ex_mem_w.rd == if_id_w.instr[24:20];\n    end\n  end\n  wire [1:0] mem_hits = match_mem & {2{ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write && !mem_misalign}};\n  wire [1:0] wb_hits  = match_wb & {2{mem_wb_w.ctrl.reg_write}};\n  assign fwd_rs1_sel = {wb_hits[0] && !mem_hits[0], mem_hits[0]};\n  assign fwd_rs2_sel = {wb_hits[1] && !mem_hits[1], mem_hits[1]};\n\n'\"'''+s[end:]\n p.write_text(s)\nr=w/'early'\ncopytree('cores/bench/rtl',r)\nearly(r)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
