{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r8s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r8s0\ntitle: Resolve register dependencies in decode and use one EX operand mux\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion selects WB write-through data at the register file, then\n  compares tags and selects a forwarding source again in EX. Gowin's\n  placement 0 worst path starts at EX/MEM.rd and reaches data RAM through\n  forwarding and the ALU. On placement 1, a register-file-to-RAM path\n  is within 0.001 ns of the limiting divider path. Both operand paths\n  cross the same forwarding network.\nhypothesis: |\n  Match each decoded source against the destinations in EX, MEM and WB\n  on the edge that issues the instruction. Capture that edge's WB data\n  once for both operands. In EX use one masked OR per operand to select\n  the EX/MEM result, MEM/WB data, issue-edge WB data or raw register-file\n  operand in that priority order. Capture a qualified MEM match and the\n  WB-vs-register-file fallback in ID. Qualify the youngest match with\n  the actual EX/MEM write permission and alignment so a trapping writer\n  exposes the next older source. Hold this metadata with ID/EX through\n  a data stall and use the divider's existing issue-time operand capture.\n  A resettable written-bit mask lets the raw 32-by-32 file use distributed\n  RAM while returning zero for x0 and unwritten registers.\n  \n  A scratch prototype reached 63.225 MHz on Gowin placement 1 against\n  60.741 MHz for the parent. It reproduced the 3,223,900 bracketed cycles,\n  all five CRCs, and the selftest and three random RVFI traces with both\n  buses stalled. Acceptance at this cycle count requires a median above\n  63.5356 MHz. Operand selection and divider timing are close enough\n  that the physical mapping of the selection logic matters.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: Infer distributed storage with per-register written bits and support raw reads while preserving standalone write-through behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Register producer matches, fallback selects and one shared WB data snapshot on ID advance. Connect qualified operand masks to EX.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Select each operand with a one-hot masked OR. Use the youngest-source bit for the existing load comparison and pointer-load bypasses.\nYAML\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
