from MEM, WB or the decoded\\nregister-file value, in that order. Register the tag match against the\\ninstruction currently in EX. In the following cycle EX needs just one\\nlate bypass, from its immediate predecessor. Preserve the specialized\\nload-to-equality-branch and LW-to-pointer-load paths. A redirect kills\\nboth younger slots. A dependency bubble holds the waiting consumer.\\n\\nThe new MEM-to-operand path makes the divider finish part of this\\nstage bound\n…[9232 of 12304 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5fe9b2c6d5e83108]…\n overflow\\nand zero divisors, including a subsequent issue with different\\nsigns or operands.\\n'}]\noutcome improvement\nfitness 218.42\ndelta_pct 15.93\nvs_baseline 1702.15\nfmax_mhz 71.51\nipc_coremark 3e-06\ncycles 3273911\niterations 10\nlut4 4117\nff 1476\nseeds [63.624, 71.51, 71.51]\nperturbations [[0, 63.624, 14], [1, 71.51, 12], [2, 71.51, 12]]\nlutram 8\nbsram 15\ndsp 2\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.ctrl.mem_read_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -10.717, 'arrival_ns': 21.012, 'logic_cells': 22, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nlogic_levels 14\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\ntimestamp 2026-11-21T17:53:11.911494Z\nslot 1\nround_id 8\nlesson - 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r8s1 (improvement, +15.93%): Collecting MEM and WB operands before EX left only the immediate predecessor to bypass in EX, and finishing division on the EX/MEM transfer edge removed two serial subtractions from the MEM forwarding path while preserving eight-cycle divide spacing.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
