{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_111","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r9s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r9s0\ntitle: Retire wrong-path replay state with the registered recovery bit\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  In the champion's 71.510 MHz placement, the path from data RAM through a\n  dependent branch to the fetch read-mode reset arrives at 19.253 ns. It is\n  only 0.026 ns behind the worst address path. A separate effective-address\n  register with parallel base additions reached 72.050 MHz on that placement.\n  The recovery signal still has to cancel several replay states on the edge\n  where the loaded branch operand first becomes available.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make the existing recovering flip-flop annul the replay response in the\n  cycle when IF presents the recovered PC. In that cycle it masks both the\n  saved word and the outstanding row and forces the effective read mode to\n  SEQUENTIAL. The raw mode, row-live bit and buffer flag can then clock\n  without the late EX redirect on their reset inputs. The recovered PC is\n  issued on the same edge schedule as today. Apply the same distinction\n  between payload and validity to bubble insertion in EX/MEM and MEM/WB.\n\n  A scratch prototype completed ten bracketed iterations in 3,273,911\n  cycles with both bus stalls, all five CRCs and the validation banner.\n  Stalled selftest and all three random retirement traces matched the ISS.\n  Gowin placement 1 rose from 71.510 to 73.707 MHz. At this cycle count\n  the qualifying median is 74.799 MHz. The outstanding timing question is\n  whether simplifying the recovery qualification at the replay and stage\n  registers can recover the remaining 1.092 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Keep raw read mode, buffer-valid and read-live state. Qualify all three\n      with recovering at use. Clear the raw buffer flag during recovery so an\n      old word cannot reappear on a prolonged stall. Select the external word\n      on ready and the replay payload otherwise. Qualify issue and prediction\n      with the full hit check. Preserve group invalidation on FENCE.I, checking\n      the fill/read collision, and the first sequential read after recovery.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Hold the EX/MEM payload on backpressure. On reset or insertion of a\n      divide bubble, clear valid, reg_write, mem_read and mem_write. Let\n      data fields capture on the ordinary stage enable so the bubble signal\n      has only the side-effect and forwarding controls as destinations.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Hold the WB payload on a data wait and clear retirement valid. Keep\n      the preceding writer eligible for collection throughout the wait.\n      On reset clear valid and the retained writer permission explicitly.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r9s0.yaml'\ny=yaml.safe_load(open(p)); jsonschema.validate(y,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(y['title'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
