o offset gives the exact index even\\nwhen the base is a freshly loaded pointer. The 1,024-entry RAM stores\\nraw words observed on the data bus and their address tags.\\n\\nRegister the predicted index beside the RAM read. In parallel, compute\\nthe exact low address bits for the external bus by using the actual\\ncarry to select either upper-slice sum. Give these bits their own\\nEX/MEM register. In MEM, qualify the word with its valid\n…[22749 of 25821 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:04cf87bdd1887ab7]…\ny instruction. Capture the formatted \noutcome regression\nfitness 231.27\ndelta_pct 5.88\nvs_baseline 1808.17\nfmax_mhz 72.613\nipc_coremark 3e-06\ncycles 3139707\niterations 10\nlut4 4402\nff 1586\nseeds [69.811, 72.613, 72.613]\nperturbations [[0, 69.811, 19], [1, 72.613, 19], [2, 72.613, 19]]\nlutram 8\nbsram 20\ndsp 2\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/g_lane[1].quotient_q_27_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_2_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.324, 'arrival_ns': 19.619, 'logic_cells': 52, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\nlogic_levels 19\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-21T18:46:31.331042Z\nslot 2\nround_id 9\nlesson - 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r9s2 (regression, +5.88%): Looking up load words during operand collection let adjacent branches and pointer loads use a registered operand in EX while MEM verified the hit, but the prototype’s 4.1% reduction in CoreMark cycles could not offset its lower median Fmax relative to the round winner (72.784 vs 78.330 MHz).\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
