experiments\nrtl\ntest\n_helpers.py\nconftest.py\ntest_alu.py\ntest_decoder.py\ntest_imm_gen.py\ntest_multiplier.py\ntest_pipeline.py\ntest_reg_file.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('r9s1'):\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\ncommand -v gw_sh\ncommand -v verilator\nls /opt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('r9s1'):\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\ncommand -v gw_sh\ncommand -v verilator\nls /opt\"","aggregated_output":"Move bypass qualification to the producer's EX cycle. For each source\nof the waiting consumer, register two enables with its collected\noperands. One selects the adjacent ALU or link result. The other\nselects an aligned adjacent load. Use the producer's actual write\npermission, including control-target faults, and its effective address\nlow bits for load alignment. A faulting producer leaves the older\nvalue from operand collection available.\n\nFor a load feeding BEQ or BNE, capture the other collected operand,\nthe producer's width and signedness, and its four-bit byte mask on\nthat same edge. In the consumer's EX cycle, compare the returned\nword in four byte lanes in parallel. Replicate the expected low byte\nor halfword across lanes and separately check that its extension\nequals the upper bits of the expected operand. Reduce equality over\nthe active lanes. This removes load formatting from the branch\ndecision while retaining formatted data for RVFI and the raw LW\nbypass for a dependent address.\n\nA scratch prototype matched all five CoreMark CRCs and the champion's\n3,273,911 marker cycles for ten iterations. Gowin placements\n0, 1 and 2 reached 71.808, 75.725 and 75.725 MHz. That median yields\n231.30 iterations/s, 5.90% above 218.42 and above the 228.47\nacceptance threshold. The added logic cost 35 LUT4s and 85 flip-flops\non placement 0. Divider feedback sets the median clock. All\n53 single-retire ALTOPS formal checks, the six cocotb suites and the\nselftest and three random RVFI traces with both bus stalls passed.\n\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/verilator\ngowin\nhwe-python\nhwe-toolchain\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
