{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrows=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))\nfor x in rows[-6:]:\n for k in ('id','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path','perturbations','seeds','hypothesis','lesson'): print(k, str(x.get(k))[:5000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "id hyp-20261121-001-r9s0\nfitness 232.89\nfmax_mhz 76.247\ncycles 3273911\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_if/initialized_initialized_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/normal_pc_7_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.814, 'arrival_ns': 18.108, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']}\nperturbations [[0, 78.039, 12], [1, 76.247, 14], [2, 76.247, 14]]\nseeds [78.039, 76.247, 76.247]\nhypothesis {'motivation': \"In the champion's 71.510 MHz placement, the path from data RAM through a\\ndependent branch to the fetch read-mode reset arrives at 19.253 ns. It is\\nonly 0.026 ns behind the worst address path. A separate effective-address\\nregister with parallel base additions reached 72.050 MHz on that placement.\\nThe recovery signal still has to cancel several replay states on the edge\\nwhere the loaded branch operand first becomes available.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Make the existing recovering flip-flop annul the replay response in the\\ncycle when IF presents the recovered PC. In that cycle it masks both the\\nsaved word and the outstanding row and forces the effective read mode to\\nSEQUENTIAL. The raw mode, row-live bit and buffer flag can then clock\\nwithout the late EX redirect on their reset inputs. The recovered PC is\\nissued on the same edge schedule as today. Apply the same distinction\\nbetween payload and validity to bubble insertion in EX/MEM and MEM/WB.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten bracketed iterations in 3,273,911\\ncycles with both bus stalls, all five CRCs and the validation banner.\\nStalled selftest and all three random retirement traces matched the ISS.\\nGowin placement 1 rose from 71.510 to 73.707 MHz. At this cycle count\\nthe qualifying median is 74.799 MHz. The outstanding timing question is\\nwhether simplifying the recovery qualification at the replay and stage\\nregisters can recover the remaining 1.092 MHz.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Keep raw read mode, buffer-valid and read-live state. Qualify all three\\nwith recovering \n…[27923 of 30995 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e20787901fe19978]…\ncent consumers. Separate internal completion from external bus\\nacceptance. Use registered demand and repair state to select the\\ncommitted load word independently of the page comparator. A pending\\nwrite has priority over any external demand.\\nDrain it before MMIO, fences, EBREAK or trap retirement. Gate all\\nfills and page training on a single eligible transfer. Exclude\\nMMIO, misaligned accesses, invalid instructions and reset.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': \"Check dynamic acquisition of several page addresses, isolated\\noutliers, replacement during a colliding lookup, both carry\\npredictions, and partial writes to cold and initialized words.\\nHold a posted store on \nlesson - 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r10s2 (regression, +6.64%): Replaying words from CoreMark’s dominant 4 KiB data page bypassed bus waits and saved 165,297 cycles over ten iterations in the prototype, while forwarding the replay RAM output through a dependent BEQ/BNE to fetch limited an early placement to 73.508 MHz.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
