{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'd=/srv/hwebench/tmp/3df75752/d464a8ce/r11-divider.xgpTjwcC\ndate -u && tail -10 \"$d/test.log\"\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json\nr=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))\nprint(r[7].get('hypothesis'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Sat Nov 21 20:02:15 UTC 2026\n..                                                                       [100%]\n2 passed in 11.14s\n{'motivation': \"On the current BTB-equipped core, Gowin traced a 28.668 ns path from\\nremainder_q to quotient_q through six dependent restoring steps. That\\npath limits the clock on all 4,043,251 CoreMark marker cycles. The\\nearlier radix-4 experiment reached 47.652 MHz on the pre-BTB core.\\nAt the champion's cycle count, a median above 45.40 MHz would clear\\nthe 4.6% acceptance margin.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Compute two quotient bits at a time inside the existing six-round\\ndivider. For each digit, form X = 4*R + the next two dividend bits.\\nSubtract D, 2D and 3D from X in parallel. The largest multiple that\\nfits gives the digit and its difference gives the next remainder.\\nThis cuts the serial remainder selections per full round from six\\nto three, while preserving the divide handshake and every instruction's\\nissue timing.\\n\\nA scratch prototype on the current core reached 44.708, 47.393 and\\n47.393 MHz on Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2. In each placement\\nthe worst path started at the register file. Option 0 used 3,297 LUT4s,\\nup from 2,985. With both bus stalls enabled, CoreMark validated all\\nfive CRCs in 4,043,251 marker cycles for ten iterations. The median\\ngives 117.22 iterations/s, 9.2% above the 107.34 champion.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 9, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Capture unsigned operand magnitudes at issue. In round one resolve\\nthe top two dividend bits with a small comparison against D=0,1,2,3\\nor D>=4, and register the full 34-bit 3D from the captured D. In\\nrounds two through six consume three radix-4 digits per round, MSB\\nfirst. Use 34-bit unsigned multiples and a 35th subtraction bit for\\nborrow. Decode mutually exclusive selects from the three fit flags\\nand select the low 32 bits of the precomputed residual directly.\\nWith f1, f2, f3 denoting fits for D, 2D, 3D, the digit bits are\\nf2 and ((f1 AND NOT f2) OR f3), MSB first. Shift the six digit\\nbits into the 32-bit combined dividend/quotient register. For D=0 every\\ndigit is three and the residual reconstructs the dividend. Preserve\\nthe signed correction, INT_MIN/-1 result, six-round done timing,\\nresult hold under backpressure and existing ALTOPS equations.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Exercise quotient and remainder one below, at and one above k*D\\nfor k=1,2,3 where the dividend fits. Include high-bit divisors for\\nwhich 2D or 3D exceeds 32 bits and dividends with alternating\\nradix-4 digits across round boundaries. Use the existing integer\\nreference and six-round handshake checks.\\n'}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor x in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if x['id'].endswith('r5s1'):\n  print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  for v in x['changes']: print(v)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor x in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if x['id'].endswith('r5s1'):\n  print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  for v in x['changes']: print(v)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Schedule the single data port one edge ahead. An older store or an\noutstanding load gets the registered address for its MEM cycle. When\nthat slot is free, decode can prepare an effective address for a younger\nload and register a grant beside ID/EX. In EX, a valid granted load to\naligned ordinary RAM can complete on the ready handshake. Its immediate\nconsumer then issues and takes the registered result from EX/MEM.\nOtherwise the load follows the existing MEM and load-use interlock.\n\nA scratch implementation completed ten CoreMark iterations in 3,288,627\nmarker cycles with both stall generators and all five canonical CRCs.\nThis saves 259,777 cycles versus the champion. Gowin placements 0, 1\nand 2 reached 48.382, 49.029 and 49.029 MHz. The median yields 149.09\niterations/s, 6.86% above 139.52. At this cycle count the acceptance\nthreshold is 47.994 MHz. Option 0 used 4,295 LUT4s and 1,092 FFs.\nSelftest and all three random programs matched the reference retirement\ntraces under both bus stalls.\n\n{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Drive io_dmemAddr directly from one clock-enabled 32-bit address\\nregister so Gowin can infer block RAM for the attached memory. Hold\\nit while an older MEM transaction waits. On advance, first reserve\\nthe next slot for an EX store or an EX load that did not complete.\\nOtherwise prepare the decoding instruction's candidate address.\\nRegister grant eligibility when ID advances and qualify use with\\nID/EX.valid, a decoded load, natural alignment and addr[31:20]==0.\\n\\nSelect the youngest nonzero base writer, EX before MEM before the\\nwrite-through register file. An ordinary EX ALU producer can supply\\na zero-displacement address. An accepted EX word load can supply\\nits returned pointer plus the new displacement. A MEM producer can\\nsupply a registered ALU/link value, a previously captured early\\nload result, or the accepted data of an aligned ordinary word load,\\nplus displacement. With no pending writer use rs1 plus the signed\\nI immediate. An unavailable youngest source disqualifies early issue.\\n\\nCapture the raw word, separately formatted byte/half/word result,\\nand completion bit on early acceptance. Use the registered formatted\\nresult on the existing EX/MEM forwarding path. Suppress the load-use\\nbubble only on acceptance. If ready is low, the same request and\\naddress continue into MEM until accepted. A completed early load\\nreleases the bus in MEM even when a younger request sees backpressure.\\n\"}\n{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': \"Expose the ordinary forwarded rs1-plus-immediate address for the\\nolder instruction's reserved slot and the fast ALU result for a\\nzero-offset base dependency. Exclude jumps, unavailable M results\\nand faulting instructions from the EX fast-base case.\\n\"}\n{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Latch the ID/EX payload on a decode advance. Apply squash and reset\\nto the valid bit and side-effect controls independently of the wide\\noperand payload, keeping the late load acceptance decision off those\\ndata inputs. Hold both on backpressure.\\n'}\n{'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'For an early-completed load, use its saved raw word with the original\\neffective address, width and sign for MEM/WB and RVFI. Suppress its\\nsecond bus request and stall. Use normal MEM handshakes for fallback\\nloads and all stores, preserving byte masks, misalignment traps,\\nMMIO ordering and one channel-zero retirement per instruction.\\n'}\n{'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Count accepted transactions and check uninterrupted EX/MEM forwarding\\nfor LW-to-branch and LW-to-load, including a nonzero displacement on\\na returned pointer. Exercise byte and halfword sign extension, a denied\\nearly read held through MEM, a stalled older store, an unavailable M\\nbase, two writers to the same base, a flushed load and a misaligned\\nload. Check exact bus addresses, masks, RVFI data and order. Assert\\nthe original bubble on fallback and adjacent retirement on an early hit.\\n'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
