{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-800\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division and remainder into a shared six-round EX divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe signed and unsigned division and remainder operators in that ALU can put\\na full 32-bit division between registers. The reference ISS retired\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers for the canonical\\n2K, -O3, ten-iteration build. It executed 93,960 MULs and zero instructions\\nfrom the DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU group. Giving just those four operations extra\\ncycles should shorten the clock period with negligible measured cycle cost.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe sig\n6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Split the six-round divider by divisor magnitude\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin traced the champion's 197-cell setup path from quotient_q[35] to\\nremainder_q[12] through six dependent 33-bit restoring steps. This limits\\nall instructions to a median 43.865 MHz, even though CoreMark retired zero\\ndivides or remainders in its 4,491,485 marker cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Gowin traced the champion's 197-cell setup path from quotient_q[35] to\\nremainder_q[12] through six dependent 33-bit restoring steps. This limits\\nall instructions to a median 43.865 MHz, even though CoreMark retired zero\\ndivides or remainders in its 4,491,485 marker cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Use two unsigned restoring datapaths under the existing s\n9:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Feed decode from a backedge-activated loop buffer during instruction stalls\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion needs 4,043,251 marker cycles for ten CoreMark iterations.\\nReplaying control transfers from its BTB already saved 154,266 cycles,\\nbut an imem stall still inserts a bubble at an arithmetic, load or store\\ninstruction, even on the next trip around the same loop. The bac\n…[5739 of 8811 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0cbf84c58e877c47]…\nd.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark executes 93,960 MUL instructions between its timing markers. The\\nchampion computes every product in MEM, so an adjacent consumer waits one\\ncycle. The placement-0 critical pat\n33:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Reuse the EX multiplier for exact reciprocal-based division\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"All three round-ten timing reports end in divider lane 1. The champion's\\ndivisor-to-remainder path crosses 48 cells, although CoreMark executes no\\ndivides between its markers. The EX multiplier is idle for all seven\\nrounds of a divide because that instruction owns EX. It can compute and\\nverify a quotient estimate within the existing retirement schedule.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"All three round-ten timing reports end in divider lane 1. The champion's\\ndivisor-to-remainder path crosses 48 cells, although CoreMark executes no\\ndivides between its markers. The EX multiplier is idle for all seven\\nrounds of a divide because that instru\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
