same loop. The backward\\nbranch gives EX a loop entry address. A single region descriptor can\\nthen identify hundreds of reusable body words in fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion needs 4,043,251 marker c\n12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Complete all RV32M results in the memory stage\", \"\n…[5391 of 8463 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5d875b7f4913d1ad]…\n0 path crosses 59 cells from quotient to remainder in\\ndivider lane 2, which performs three dependent 18-bit restores per clock.\\nCoreMark executes zero divides or remainders between its markers, so the\\ndivider can raise the score by shortening the clock period. At that cycle\\ncount the acceptance threshold is a median just above 88.91 MHz.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivati\n39:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Prepare execution operands and PC-relative results in collection\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion's median Gowin placement traces EX/MEM result bit 0 through\\naddress alignment and writer qualification to the next instruction's\\n32-bit operand register. A second path, only 0.004 ns shorter, goes\\nthrough the integer ALU into the EX/MEM result. At 3,044,309 cycles\\nfor ten iterations, 96.48 MHz is sufficient to clear the 4.6% margin.\\nEliminating every remaining bubble could gain only 4.19% at today's clock.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion's median Gowin placem\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
