y completes, then re-execute. An advancing alignment fault\n  uses the champion's flush and refetch. The expected cycle count is\n  3,044,309, requiring a median above 101.734 MHz to qualify. The main\n  timing risk is the producer-to-operand register path through the low\n  product or integer result selection.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Make the integer result, low product, link PC and formatted load\n      candidate available in parallel to the operand capture logic.\n      Keep the corresponding EX/MEM result for architectural writeback.\n      Drive rs1 and rs2 from the captured values for comparisons, address\n      generation, the DSP, stores and RVFI. Select PC and immediate by\n      operand role for the integer ALU.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Build one collection result per source from the four masked producer\n      classes and the existing youngest eligible fallback. Qualify the\n      producer's class enables with each adjacent match before merging\n      data. Capture on \"'!stall_ex. Retain the adjacent-load repair mask,\n      correct each matched port once on repair && !mem_wait, and preserve\n      redirect priority, x0 and the late-result interlock.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Follow MUL by an ADD that reads its result twice and require\n      consecutive retirements. Repeat with a cold LW held by dmemReady,\n      older writes to the same rd and both ADD sources matching the load.\n      Check the single accepted read, both corrected RVFI source values,\n      final sum and one retirement per instruction.\nYAML\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r14s1.yaml')\nv=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(v,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(v['title'])\nPY\