{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r1s1.yaml && ls -la cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && git check-ignore -v cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r1s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Move division and remainder into a shared six-round EX divider\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\n  The signed and unsigned division and remainder operators in that ALU can put\n  a full 32-bit division between registers. CoreMark repeatedly multiplies in\n  its matrix kernel, while its variable-divisor work appears concentrated in\n  setup and reporting. Charging extra cycles only to DIV and REM should buy\n  substantially more clock frequency than it costs in bracketed cycles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one blocking divider in EX. Capture forwarded\n  operand magnitudes and sign flags on issue. Zero-extend the dividend to 36\n  bits and consume six bits per clock for six clocks with six cascaded binary\n  restoring steps. Register the partial quotient and remainder after each\n  group. On the following clock select and sign-correct the result into\n  EX/MEM. This adds seven cycles per divide with a ready bus and keeps the\n  ordinary ALU and multiply paths single-cycle. With the baseline's 4,491,485\n  measured cycles, a 1% cycle increase would require just over 5.75 MHz to\n  clear the 4.6% acceptance margin. Check both median Fmax and marker cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace all four combinational divide/remainder cases with the shared\n      clocked recurrence. Use a 33-bit trial subtraction per restoring step.\n      Latch the quotient sign from both operands and the remainder sign from\n      the dividend. Return all ones or the original dividend on division by\n      zero and the defined quotient or remainder for INT_MIN divided by -1.\n      Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS carry the existing per-op substitute result\n      through the same issue, busy and completion timing as real division.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Launch once from a valid divide when EX/MEM can advance. Capture both\n      forwarded source values for RVFI before older bypass values drain.\n      Keep the instruction in ID/EX and inject a completely inert EX/MEM\n      bubble on each waiting cycle that MEM can accept. On completion write\n      the result through the existing EX/MEM forwarding and retirement path\n      exactly once. Hold completed data until accepted and clear busy on reset.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Hold the fetch PC and ID/EX while a divide waits. Let older work drain\n      normally. Give a stalled older dmem transaction priority over inserting\n      an EX/MEM bubble, and release the front end when EX transfers the result.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire divider backpressure from EX to the hazard unit independently of\n      the existing MEM stall so an older load or store can complete.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Drive divide vectors through the clocked request and completion interface\n      with a timeout. Retain all arithmetic checks and compare full-width\n      signed and unsigned operands against an integer reference.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a stalled older load feeding a divide, a dependent consumer,\n      consecutive divides, and a divide flushed by a taken branch. Check\n      forwarded values, RVFI source data and order, and single retirement.\ntotal 20\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 21 14:15 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody    nogroup   4096 Nov 21 14:14 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 3442 Nov 21 14:15 hyp-20261121-002-r1s1.yaml\n.gitignore:88:cores/*/experiments/hypotheses/\tcores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r1s1.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
