{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|197 cells|divider' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Resolve four quotient bits per step in the combinational divider\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline ran at a median 5.442 MHz. Gowin reported a 199.837 ns path\\nthrough forwarding and the EX ALU. The single-cycle 32-bit division and\\nremainder operators are likely sources of that depth. They constrain the\\nclock even on cycles when CoreMark executes an add or a load.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline ran at a median 5.442 MHz. Gowin reported a 199.837 ns path\\nthrough forwarding and the EX ALU. The single-cycle 32-bit division and\\nremainder operators are likely sources of that depth. They constrain the\\nclock even on cycles when CoreMark executes an add or a load.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one combinational radix-16 restoring\\ndivider. Starting with remainder zero, consume the unsigned dividend from\\nthe most significant nibble in eight steps. At each step append the next\\nnibble to the remainder and try the 15 nonzero multiples of the divisor\\nin parallel. The largest multiple that fits gives both the quotient digit\\nand the residual to carry into the next step. Eight serial digit decisions\\nshorten the EX path while retaining single-cycle execution and forwarding.\\nA scratch prototype reached 6.324, 6.907 and 6.907 MHz on Gowin placement\\noptions 0, 1 and 2. It passed 13,588 arithmetic comparisons and validated\\nall CoreMark CRCs in the baseline's 4,491,485 bracketed cycles. The median\\nclock gives 15.38 iterations/s, a 26.9% gain over 12.12 iterations/s.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 27, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Share a bank of 36-bit shift/add multiples of the divisor magnitude.\\nIn step i (1 through 8), the dividend prefix bounds the trial width\\nto W = 4*i bits. Subtract each multiple's low W bits with a borrow\\nbit and independently check its upper bits for zero. Combine those\\ntests into fit flags. Use adjacent flags to one-hot select\n…[15712 of 18784 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:88db1070012a468b]…\ngression\", \"fitness\": 13.06, \"delta_pct\": 7.76, \"vs_baseline\": 7.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.488, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4203476, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12320, \"ff\": 527, \"seeds\": [5.336, 5.488, 5.488], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.336, 149], [1, 5.488, 146], [2, 5.488, 146]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -182.391, \"arrival_ns\": 192.685, \"logic_cells\": 160, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 149, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T13:28:39.598646Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.76%): Predicting branches with 32 two-bit counters and steering JALs in fetch avoided one-cycle EX redirects and cut CoreMark cycles by 6.4%, but the combinational EX divider kept Fmax near 5.5 MHz versus 43.9 MHz with multicycle division.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
