{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nprint(list(d[-1]))\nfor k in [2,4,5,7,8,9]:\n x=d[k]\n for f in x:\n  if f in ('id','title','category','implementation_notes','timing','fmax_mhz','hypothesis','notes','summary','coremark_cycles','worst_path'): print(f, str(x[f])[:4500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\nid hyp-20261121-002-r1s1\ntitle Move division and remainder into a shared six-round EX divider\ncategory structural\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe signed and unsigned division and remainder operators in that ALU can put\\na full 32-bit division between registers. The reference ISS retired\\n2,922,015 instructions strictly between the timing markers for the canonical\\n2K, -O3, ten-iteration build. It executed 93,960 MULs and zero instructions\\nfrom the DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU group. Giving just those four operations extra\\ncycles should shorten the clock period with negligible measured cycle cost.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one blocking divider in EX. Capture forwarded\\noperand magnitudes and sign flags on issue. Zero-extend the dividend to 36\\nbits and consume six bits per clock for six clocks with six cascaded binary\\nrestoring steps. Register the partial quotient and remainder after each\\ngroup. On the following clock select and sign-correct the result into\\nEX/MEM. This adds seven cycles per divide with a ready bus and keeps the\\nordinary ALU and multiply paths single-cycle. At the baseline's 4,491,485\\nmarker cycles, a median Fmax above 5.70 MHz clears the acceptance margin\\nand 8.17 MHz delivers the forecast 50% fitness gain. Measure both because\\nextra cycles before the start marker can shift the pseudo-random bus stalls.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 50, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Replace all four combinational divide/remainder cases with the shared\\nclocked recurrence.\n…[17805 of 20877 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cd18077a1d2bb76e]…\ning EX-to-IF connection.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export advancing and the resolved aligned transfer direction. Use the\\nexisting BTB write qualification to identify an anchor. Allow a successor\\npayload write for a decoded legal non-branch, non-jump instruction at an\\naligned RAM PC on EX advance. FENCE.I invalidation overrides the write.\\nKeep recovery and RVFI next PC driven by the full architectural resolution.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm a loop and withhold imem throughout its body, including across a\\nload-use interlock and a four-cycle dmem hold. Check that a 17-word body\\ncan replay the first 16 and must wait for word 17. Change branch direction,\\nalias two source branches to one index and retarget a JALR with a store\\non the old path. Check the RVFI PC pairs and store strobes. Execute\\nFENCE.I, revisit the same branch and require its first successor to wait\\nfor the replacement instruction on the bus.\\n'}]}\nfmax_mhz 42.974\nimplementation_notes \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
