{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_32", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r4s2','r5s2')):\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  for c in r['changes']: print(c['file'], c['description'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Use a 4,096-entry, direct-mapped table of instruction words and next-PC\npredictions. Present the selected next PC to synchronous RAM on the same\nedge that installs it in the PC register. Each tagged word can serve an\nimem wait regardless of which branch led to it. Conditional branches in\nthe same aligned 16 KiB region get independent targets and two-bit\ndirection counters. Jumps predict their last resolved aligned target.\n\nA scratch RTL prototype cut the unavailable-fetch count to 439 and EX\nredirects from 62,551 to 41,173. Ten iterations took 3,359,136 marker\ncycles with both stall generators enabled and all five CRCs matching.\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 43.307, 43.269 and 43.269 MHz.\nThe median gives 128.81 iterations/s, 5.26% above the champion. The\nacceptance threshold at this cycle count is about 42.997 MHz. Option\nzero used 3,595 LUT4s and 23 BSRAMs. The prototype passed all 53\nsingle-retirement formal checks and matched the reference on selftest\nand all three random programs with both stall generators enabled.\n\nrtl/if_stage.sv Replace the branch-indexed paths and their cursors with one synchronous\nlookup per fetch. Index by PC[13:2], store PC[19:14] as a tag, and check\nthe full aligned RAM range. Pack the tag, control flag, existing\ntwo-bit counter, target[19:2] and instruction into each 59-bit word.\nDeclare a flat vector array with one synchronous write port and a\nsynchronous read into a vector register so Gowin infers block RAM.\nInstall a control entry on update.write or a sequential entry on\nupdate.successor. Both signals already qualify EX advancement.\n\nDrive the RAM read address from the next PC. Reset selects zero, EX\nrecovery overrides a hold, and a held fetch rereads its current PC.\nSet prediction.hit only for tagged control hits. On acceptance,\nselect the saved target when the counter MSB is set and the selected\nword is a legal control transfer. Otherwise advance to PC+4. A ready\nexternal instruction wins. A stalled miss presents an invalid NOP.\nEX compares the prediction carried w\n…[3745 of 6817 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:daca33d2fb3c8819]…\n recovery. Disable the table hit then. For other cycles require\nthe full aligned RAM PC tag, live group, initialized slot and clean\nread. A ready external word wins. A stalled miss presents an invalid\nNOP. Predict taken only for a control entry with the counter MSB set\nand a legal control encoding when consuming an external word. Pass\nthe selected prediction through the existing ID/EX snapshot for EX\ndirection and full-target checking, trap handling and FENCE.I recovery.\n\ntest/test_pipeline.py Require word 17 in the trained loop to advance with imem held low.\nIn the two-word loop, supply a changed body instruction on the second\nlap and withhold imem from the third. Its write collides with the\npredicted target read. Check the one-cycle retry and the new value.\nExercise two PCs 8 KiB apart, a cold slot in a live group and refill\nafter FENCE.I. For a retargeted JALR behind a held load, check both\nready and stalled fetches at the corrected PC, link data, exact RVFI\nPC pairs and the absence of wrong-path stores.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat > \"$TMPDIR/r6s1/banks.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os,sys\nt=Path(os.environ['TMPDIR'])/'r6s1'\ns=Path('cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv').read_text()\np=s.index('  // EX consumes')\nst=s.index('  logic        want_rem_q',p)\nen=s.index('  logic [29:0] remainder_next;',p)\na=s[st:en]\na='  logic [31:0] dividend_abs, divisor_abs, divisor_q;\\\\n'+a\na += '''\n  assign divisor_abs = negative_b ? -b : b;\n  logic [1:0] tail_q;\n  logic zero_q;\n  logic [31:0] zero_result_q;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (div_start) begin\n      divisor_q <= divisor_abs;\n      tail_q <= dividend_abs[1:0];\n      want_rem_q <= want_rem;\n      negate_q <= want_rem ? negative_a : negative_a \"'^ negative_b;\n      zero_q <= b==0;\n      zero_result_q <= want_rem ? a : 32'\"'hffff_ffff;\n    end\n  end\n'''\nspeeds=[int(i) for i in sys.argv[1].split(',')]\nlimits=[30 - 6*k for k in speeds]+[30]\nnames=[]\nfor i,rate in enumerate(speeds):\n  w=limits[i+1]\n  qi=rate*6\n  n=f'lane{rate}'\n  names.append(n)\n  a+=f'''\n  logic [{w-1}:0] {n}_r;\n  logic [{qi-1}:0] {n}_q;\n  logic [{w}:0] {n}_rnext;\n  logic [{w+1}:0] {n}_trial;\n  logic [{rate-1}:0] {n}_digits;\n  logic {n}_sel;\n  always_comb begin\n    {n}_rnext = {{1'b0,{n}_r}};\n    for (int i=0;i<{rate};i++) begin\n      {n}_rnext = {{{n}_rnext[{w-1}:0],{n}_q[{qi-1}-i]}};\n      {n}_trial = {{1'b0,{n}_rnext}} - {{2'b0,divisor_q[{w-1}:0]}};\n      {n}_digits[{rate-1}-i] = \"'!{n}_trial[{w+1}];\n      if ({n}_digits[{rate-1}-i]) {n}_rnext = {n}_trial[{w}:0];\n    end\n  end\n'\"'''\n  seed=limits[i]\n  rinit=\\\"'0\\\" if seed==0 else f\\\"{{{w-seed}'b0,dividend_abs[31:{32-seed}]}}\\\"\n  good=f\\\"\"'!(|divisor_abs[31:{w}])\"\n  if seed: good+=f\" && (|divisor_abs[31:{seed}])\"\n  if i==len(speeds)-1: good=f\"(|divisor_abs[31:{seed}])\"\n  high=f\" && !(|divisor_q[31:{w}])\" if i==len(speeds)-1 else '\"''\n  if high: a=a.replace(f\\\"= \"'!{n}_trial[{w+1}];\",f\"= !{n}_trial[{w+1}]{high};\")\n  a+=f'\"'''\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (div_start) begin\n      {n}_r <= {rinit};\n      {n}_q <= dividend_abs[{qi+1}:2];\n      {n}_sel <= {good};\n    end else if (div_busy && \"'!div_done) begin\n      {n}_r <= {n}_rnext[{w-1}:0];\n      {n}_q <= {{{n}_q[{qi-rate-1}:0],{n}_digits}};\n    end\n  end'\"'''\nmake=lambda n,f,sw : f\\\"({{{{30{{{n}_sel}}}}}} & \\\"+(f\\\"{{{30-sw}'b0,{n}_{f}}}\\\" if sw<30 else f\\\"{n}_{f}\\\")+\\\")\\\"\nfor f in ('q','r'):\n sig='quotient_q' if f=='q' else 'remainder_q'\n a+=\\\"\\\\n  wire [29:0] \\\"+sig+\\\" = \\\"+\\\" | \\\".join(make(n,f,6*speeds[i] if f=='q' else limits[i+1]) for i,n in enumerate(names))+\\\";\\\\n\\\"\na+=s[s.index('  // MEM reads'):s.index('\"'`endif'\"',p)].replace('assign div_result = negate_q ?', 'assign div_result = zero_q ? zero_result_q : negate_q ?')\n(t/'rtl/alu.sv').write_text(s[:p]+a+s[s.index('\"'`endif'\"',p):])\nPY\npython \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/r6s1/banks.py\" 5,3,1 && PYTHONPATH=. python \"$TMPDIR/r6s1/timing.py\" banks 0 1 2'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
