{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r2s0','r3s0')): print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\nls '/srv/hwebench/tmp/3df75752/aca414f5/r8s1.3LJjRpnZ/p-rf16/gowin_p1/impl/pnr'\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261121-001-r2s0 Replace each pair of binary restoring steps with one radix-4 digit.\nFor each digit, append two dividend bits to the partial remainder and\nsubtract D, 2D and 3D in parallel, where D is the divisor magnitude.\nUse the borrow flags to select the largest multiple that fits, its\ntwo-bit digit, and its already-computed residual. Resolve the top two\ndividend bits in round one and six bits in each of the next five rounds.\nKeep the current six-round protocol in hardware and ALTOPS.\n\nA scratch RTL prototype reached 46.988, 47.706 and 47.706 MHz on Gowin\nplacement options 0, 1 and 2. CoreMark validated all five CRCs in\n4,491,485 bracketed cycles for ten iterations. The measured median gives\n106.21 iterations/s, 8.76% above the 97.66 champion. Option 0 used\n3,048 LUT4s against the champion's 2,756. All three worst paths now\nstart at the register file.\n\nhyp-20261121-001-r3s0 Compute two quotient bits at a time inside the existing six-round\ndivider. For each digit, form X = 4*R + the next two dividend bits.\nSubtract D, 2D and 3D from X in parallel. The largest multiple that\nfits gives the digit and its difference gives the next remainder.\nThis cuts the serial remainder selections per full round from six\nto three, while preserving the divide handshake and every instruction's\nissue timing.\n\nA scratch prototype on the current core reached 44.708, 47.393 and\n47.393 MHz on Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2. In each placement\nthe worst path started at the register file. Option 0 used 3,297 LUT4s,\nup from 2,985. With both bus stalls enabled, CoreMark validated all\nfive CRCs in 4,043,251 marker cycles for ten iterations. The median\ngives 117.22 iterations/s, 9.2% above the 107.34 champion.\n\ncmd.do\ncore_bench.bin\ncore_bench.binx\ncore_bench.db\ncore_bench.fs\ncore_bench.log\ncore_bench.pin.html\ncore_bench.power.html\ncore_bench.rpt.html\ncore_bench.rpt.txt\ncore_bench.timing_paths\ncore_bench.tr\ncore_bench.tr.html\ncore_bench_tr_cata.html\ncore_bench_tr_content.html\ndevice.cfg\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
