{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r8s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261121-002-r8s1\ntitle: Give loads and stores a dedicated registered address path\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,223,900 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Its\n  reported Gowin path starts at EX/MEM.rd, crosses forwarding and the\n  general EX ALU, and ends at the data RAM. Loads and stores need just\n  a base plus an immediate, yet their address passes through the same\n  result selection as shifts, logical operations and jump links.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the load/store address generator from the integer result bus at\n  the EX/MEM boundary. Compute a full-width base-plus-displacement with\n  a dedicated adder. Select the base from the captured rs1, the two\n  forwarding buses or the raw memory word on the existing LW-to-load\n  bypass. Register the address directly for the MEM bus and use its\n  low bits for alignment and byte lanes. All requests still issue in\n  MEM with the existing handshake. This should shorten the path to data\n  RAM with the same dependency penalties and marker cycle count. At\n  that cycle count the acceptance threshold is about 63.54 MHz, versus\n  the champion's median of 60.741 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add a 32-bit effective address to the EX/MEM payload.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Form and register the effective address independently of the ALU\n      and link result mux. Honor the youngest eligible rs1 writer and\n      select raw dmem data only for the existing aligned LW-to-load\n      dependency. Hold the address with its request under backpressure.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the registered effective address for dmem, misalignment, lane\n      masks, load extraction and the aligned RVFI address. Retain the\n      current writeback and trap rules.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check a load/store base written by two successive instructions and\n      an LW-to-load pointer chain held across dmem waits. Check effective\n      addresses, byte masks, returned values and retirement order.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
