{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]\nprint(rows[-1].keys())\nfor row in rows[-3:]:\n print(str(row)[:9000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n{'id': 'hyp-20261121-001-r9s0', 'title': 'Retire wrong-path replay state with the registered recovery bit', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'motivation': \"In the champion's 71.510 MHz placement, the path from data RAM through a\\ndependent branch to the fetch read-mode reset arrives at 19.253 ns. It is\\nonly 0.026 ns behind the worst address path. A separate effective-address\\nregister with parallel base additions reached 72.050 MHz on that placement.\\nThe recovery signal still has to cancel several replay states on the edge\\nwhere the loaded branch operand first becomes available.\\n\", 'hypothesis': {'motivation': \"In the champion's 71.510 MHz placement, the path from data RAM through a\\ndependent branch to the fetch read-mode reset arrives at 19.253 ns. It is\\nonly 0.026 ns behind the worst address path. A separate effective-address\\nregister with parallel base additions reached 72.050 MHz on that placement.\\nThe recovery signal still has to cancel several replay states on the edge\\nwhere the loaded branch operand first becomes available.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Make the existing recovering flip-flop annul the replay response in the\\ncycle when IF presents the recovered PC. In that cycle it masks both the\\nsaved word and the outstanding row and forces the effective read mode to\\nSEQUENTIAL. The raw mode, row-live bit and buffer flag can then clock\\nwithout the late EX redirect on their reset inputs. The recovered PC is\\nissued on the same edge schedule as today. Apply the same distinction\\nbetween payload and validity to bubble insertion in EX/MEM and MEM/WB.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten bracketed iterations in 3,273,\n…[20290 of 23362 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:790f51132454199f]…\nstanding bus miss holds its address until acceptance.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Start the lookup from the waiting slot. Select an unverified preceding\\nLW word for a pointer chain, an older registered ALU or load candidate,\\nWB data, or the saved base. Latch metadata only with its instruction.\\nRecord each adjacent source match together with the EX producer's\\nnonzero destination and trap-qualified write permission.\\nLet an adjacent consumer enter EX behind a load. If the load misses,\\nhold that consumer and the front end, drain the accepted load once,\\ninject an EX/MEM bubble and replace matching operands with accepted\\ndata. A misaligned producer preserves the saved older operand. Verify\\nboth source matches, x0, reset, flush and divider ownership. Keep\\nexternal requests on exact addresses. Compute low address candidates\\nfor the collected base and the adjacent forwarded value, select the\\ntrue sum into a dedicated register for port bits [12:2], and hold it\\nwith EX/MEM. Stores and MMIO\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
