{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_88", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r10s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-003-r10s2\ntitle: \"Predict the active data page for word replay\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's ten-iteration retirement trace contains 544,852 loads.\n  A 256-entry PC-stride model selected a reusable word for 255,815 of\n  them. Page locality was much stronger. Of the 684,483 load and store\n  retirements between markers, 678,641 addressed one aligned 4 KiB page.\n  This suggests learning one page tag for 1,024 words. It removes the\n  per-word address tags and the collection-stage forwarded-base lookup\n  of the round-nine predictor.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict that a memory access will use the currently resident page.\n  Learn its tag from resolved ordinary-RAM accesses. Retain it across\n  isolated excursions and replace it after two consecutive references\n  to the same competing page. Probe a synchronous word RAM in EX using\n  only the page offset. Predict the carry into bit 6 from displacement\n  bit 5 so the two offset slices can add in parallel. In MEM, compare\n  the probe index with the exact word offset and check the full physical\n  page, initialized bit, load alignment and absence of a write collision.\n\n  A verified load supplies the raw word for forwarding and retirement.\n  A resident store updates the same word's enabled bytes and can place\n  its exact address, data and mask in one ordered write-through slot.\n  This keeps the predictor coherent while allowing later verified loads\n  to proceed during a bus wait. A miss uses the exact external address.\n  Keep the external RAM address registered so Gowin can infer block RAM.\n\n  A scratch version with a registered external address completed ten\n  iterations in 3,096,266 marker cycles with both stalls, all five expected\n  CRCs and the validation banner. The champion took 3,273,911 cycles.\n  At that cycle count the candidate needs a median above 77.49 MHz to\n  clear the acceptance margin. Preserving clock speed is the main risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/page_predictor.sv\n    description: |\n      Track a resident and a challenger page. Make replacement atomic by\n      clearing a 64-bit group-live vector. On the first whole-word fill\n      in a group, replace its 16-bit initialization mask. Install an\n      accepted RAM load or a whole-word store. A partial store may update\n      initialized bytes but cannot make an unknown word readable. Reject\n      same-index RAM read/write collisions. Hold each response and its\n      index together on backpressure. Keep the write-through transaction\n      stable until handshake and allow simultaneous drain and replacement.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the forwarded base, including the adjacent raw LW pointer, to\n      generate the predicted offset for the synchronous read. Produce\n      bits 5 through 2 from the low six-bit sum and bits 11 through 6\n      from an independent six-bit sum with the predicted carry. Preserve\n      the exact effective address for identity, byte lanes and faults.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Integrate the page prediction with memory backpressure and the EX\n      bypass. Route the selected raw word to MEM formatting, RVFI and\n      adjacent consumers. Separate internal completion from external bus\n      acceptance. A pending write has priority over any external demand.\n      Drain it before MMIO, fences, EBREAK or trap retirement. Gate all\n      fills and page training on a single eligible transfer. Exclude\n      MMIO, misaligned accesses, invalid instructions and reset.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check dynamic acquisition of several page addresses, isolated\n      outliers, replacement during a colliding lookup, both carry\n      predictions, and partial writes to cold and initialized words.\n      Hold a posted store on an unready bus while issuing a same-word\n      load and another store. Check exact bus write order, marker and\n      fence ordering, and every load's full retirement record.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
