{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r8s2','r9s2','r10s0','r10s2')):\n  print(r['id'], r['cycles'],r['critical_path'],r['hypothesis'], r['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-003-r8s2 3078813 {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_1_s0', 'to': 'dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -13.267, 'arrival_ns': 23.562, 'logic_cells': 24, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} {'motivation': 'A marker-bracketed trace of the champion counted 191,317 data-bus stall\\ncycles, 45,890 redirects and 19,787 cycles without a fetch word over ten\\nCoreMark iterations. The 544,852 loads give a word-address predictor a\\nlarger opportunity than further improvements to branch direction. A\\nPC-stride load predictor saved only 39,881 cycles in a scratch run.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Predict the carry into effective-address bit 6 to start a synchronous\\nload-word lookup in EX. Form the low six address bits and the next six\\nbits in parallel. Use displacement bit 5 as the predicted carry between\\nthe slices. This predicts zero carry for small positive offsets and one\\nfor small negative offsets. A zero offset gives the exact index even\\nwhen the base is a freshly loaded pointer. The 1,024-entry RAM stores\\nraw words observed on the data bus and their address tags.\\n\\nRegister the predicted index beside the RAM read. In parallel, compute\\nthe exact low address bits for the external bus by using the actual\\ncarry to select either upper-slice sum. Give these bits their own\\nEX/MEM register. In MEM, qualify the word with its valid bit, full address,\\nordinary-RAM range, natural alignment and write-collision status. An\\naccepted bus read supplies the live word. During backpressure a\\nverified prediction can supply the same word and complete the load.\\nA wrong carry or tag costs the usual memory wait. Full-word stores\\ninstall their data and partial stores invalidate the indexed word.\\n\\nA scratch RTL prototype took 3,078,813 marker cycles versus 3,223,900\\nfor the champion with both stall generators, all five canonical CRCs\\nand the validation banner. This saves 145,087 cycles. It needs median\\nGowin Fmax above 60.6763 MHz to clear 197.07686 iterations/s. That\\nnarrow timing margin\n…[18955 of 22027 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6c344c7754c2447e]…\n'description': 'Integrate the page prediction with memory backpressure and the EX\\nbypass. Route the selected raw word to MEM formatting, RVFI and\\nadjacent consumers. Separate internal completion from external bus\\nacceptance. Use registered demand and repair state to select the\\ncommitted load word independently of the page comparator. A pending\\nwrite has priority over any external demand.\\nDrain it before MMIO, fences, EBREAK or trap retirement. Gate all\\nfills and page training on a single eligible transfer. Exclude\\nMMIO, misaligned accesses, invalid instructions and reset.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': \"Check dynamic acquisition of several page addresses, isolated\\noutliers, replacement during a colliding lookup, both carry\\npredictions, and partial writes to cold and initialized words.\\nHold a posted store on an unready bus while issuing a same-word\\nload and another store. Check exact bus write order, marker and\\nfence ordering, and every load's full retirement record.\\n\"}]} \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
