rly guess without issuing an external read. Capture late\\neligibility in EX using an initialized-sector bit. Require every word in\\nthe sector to be known before enabling this shortcut. Independently\\ninitialized words can still satisfy the early probe. If an adjacent\\nconsumer used an incorrect early prediction, annul its effects, hold\\nit in EX, and capture the verified late value or the accepted bus value\\ninto each matching operand. Re-execute it once. Independent consumers\\ncontinue\n…[14565 of 17637 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:790a538837aad379]…\naccepts A. Reuse one unsigned high-product circuit\\nin rounds three and five. In rounds four and six use a second multiply-add\\npath to compute the low word of R+E*(-D) from a registered -D.\\nSave the first E on round four and sum both estimates on round\\nsix. Register the corrected quotient and remainder on div_last.\\nKeep these arithmetic paths local to the divider so ordinary MUL\\nretains its EX/MEM bypass. Preserve ALTOPS, the seven-round\\nhandshake, backpressure, consecutive divides and reset behavior.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': \"Check the error inequality at each nonempty bucket's minimum D\\nbelow H/2 using g=H-D*M and g*D+g*g < H*D. Exercise actual RTL\\nat bucket edges, with maximum dividends, exact multiples and their\\nneighbors. Include a first estimate that misses by hundreds and\\ncases that use the final increment. Compare all four DIV/REM\\noperations with the integer reference, including divide by zero,\\nsigned overflow and a result held across downstream stalls.\\n\"}]}\n\nNone\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
