{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r10s0','r11s0')):\n  print(d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': \"MUL pays the same adjacent-consumer bubble as MULH even though its low\\n32 bits fit the existing EX/MEM forwarding register. Gowin also traces\\nthe champion's placement 0 setup limit from EX/MEM.alu_op[2] through\\nthe MEM multiplier to a collected operand. In the median placement a\\nsimilar multiply path arrives only 0.007 ns before the limiting path.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Move the existing DSP multiply to EX. Give the low product a dedicated\\nenable in the ordinary EX result mux so the next instruction can use\\nit through the existing bypass. Capture the high product separately at\\nEX/MEM and select it in MEM for MULH, MULHU and MULHSU. This removes the\\nlive DSP output from operand collection and saves the dependency bubble\\non MUL. Decode the result enables in collection so adding the low product\\ncosts one input to the EX result reduction. In paired placement-1 trials\\nthe cascaded ALU/link/product mux reached 79.211 MHz. Forming the eleven\\nmasked integer terms inside the ALU, then ORing its output with the enabled\\nPC+4 and low product in EX reached 83.677 MHz.\\n\\nThe scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,238,429 bracketed\\ncycles with both bus stalls, saving 35,482 cycles. All five CRCs and the\\nvalidation banner matched. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 79.634,\\n83.677 and 83.677 MHz. The 83.677 MHz median gives 258.39 iterations/s,\\n7.99% above 239.26. The qualifying median is 81.047 MHz.\\nPlacement 0 used 3,892 LUT4s, 1,413 registers and two DSPs.\\nAll 53 ALTOPS formal checks and all six cocotb suites passed. Selftest\\nand the three random programs matched the reference with and without stalls.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 8, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry eleven ordinary ALU result enables, a low and a high multiply\\nenable, and two multiply signedness flags into EX. Carry the high\\nproduct and the high-product, divide and ordinary writeback enables\\nin ex_mem_t.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'descripti\n…[5381 of 8453 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:35b6f9f29a14e04c]…\niate.\\nUse the original result enables for instructions that write an\\nALU result. Reconstruct full trace operands using the trace snapshots,\\noriginal adjacent matches, fault qualification and formatted load\\nresult, including operands held over a divide.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add raw source values and raw adjacent-match metadata for RVFI to\\nid_ex_t. Keep one pair of timing-visible collected data operands.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Initialize the added trace fields in the decode payload. Collection\\nfills them from the youngest eligible writers at transfer.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise an OP-IMM whose immediate bits name the preceding writer\\nand an AUIPC whose encoded rs1 bits name that writer. Check rd_wdata\\nand both raw RVFI operands. Follow an adjacent producer with a store\\nwhose displacement and forwarded data differ, hold the bus unready,\\nand check the accepted address, byte lanes, write data and retirement.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
