{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r13s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Predict the upper-half carry on the integer result bypass\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion retires 2,922,016 instructions in 3,044,309 CoreMark marker\n  cycles. Even perfect issue at 92.229 MHz would gain only 4.19%, below\n  the 4.6% acceptance margin. Its placement-0 timing report follows an EX\n  PC bit through the ALU to bit 29 of the result register. Predicting the\n  carry at bit 16 lets a dependent instruction use a sum after two\n  parallel half-width additions. The existing load repair path already\n  provides a way to retry a consumer of an incorrect bypass value.\nhypothesis: |\n  For ADD, ADDI, AUIPC and SUB, compute the low 16-bit sum and its true\n  carry in parallel with the high 16-bit sum. For subtraction use\n  A + ~B + 1. Predict the carry into bit 16 from a short window immediately\n  below the boundary. For example, add A[15:12] and Y[15:12] with Y[11]\n  as the seed, where Y is B for addition and ~B for subtraction. Use the\n  window carry for the upper sum. On a small sign-extended displacement\n  this seed also predicts a carry across a long run of propagating bits.\n\n  Register the predicted sum on the existing adjacent bypass. Capture the\n  true and predicted carry on the same transfer. They determine an exact\n  correction of zero, plus one or minus one in the high half, modulo\n  2^16. MEM supplies the corrected full word to writeback and older-source\n  forwarding. When a valid adjacent consumer used a wrong sum, reuse the\n  existing load-miss repair cycle to replace every matching operand and\n  re-execute the consumer before any side effect. An independent successor\n  continues at full rate. Carry comparison and correction are outside\n  the EX sum-to-bypass path. The acceptance target at the original cycle\n  count is a median above 96.48 MHz. Measure carry misses that actually\n  replay a consumer and recompute that target from the new marker count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement the split EX sum, local carry predictor and exact lower\n      carry. Share the circuit across integer addition and subtraction.\n      Preserve exact combinational ALU results for its existing standalone\n      interface if exposing a separate speculative result to EX.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Carry the qualified arithmetic carry metadata with its producer in\n      EX/MEM. A valid arithmetic writer to a nonzero rd can require repair.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Select the predicted integer sum into the normal result register\n      and latch the carries alongside it. Preserve exact effective\n      addresses, jump targets, link values and comparisons. Apply the\n      existing repair interlock to redirects, training and EX/MEM transfer.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Reconstruct the exact upper half using the saved carry difference.\n      Select the corrected value for MEM/WB and collection forwarding,\n      including when the next instruction has no dependency.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend adjacent-load validation to recognize a producer with an\n      incorrect predicted carry. Hold and repair both matching operand\n      slots from MEM, clear their bypass enables and execute exactly once.\n      Qualify the check with valid producer and consumer transfers and\n      preserve its ownership through memory waits, redirects and reset.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Force both directions of carry error, including SUB with a borrow.\n      Test dependent branches, stores, dual-source consumers, back-to-back\n      speculative adds and an independent successor. Check retirement\n      values, source operands and bus effects under backpressure.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
