{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrows=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))\nfor r in rows[-3:-1]:\n print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],r['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261121-001-r13s0 Record the two adjacent RAW matches when a producer moves from\ncollection into EX and the following instruction moves from decode into\ncollection. For each source compare its decode address to the producer's\nnonzero rd and qualify the match with producer validity and decoded\nreg_write. Drive operand selection from those registered matches and EX\nvalidity. This removes address generation and trap checking from the\npath that zeros the saved value and selects the adjacent bypass.\n\nA load or link instruction can still lose its write permission in EX.\nIf its data or link alignment check fails and a waiting source matches,\nuse the existing late-result interlock for one issue bubble. Let the\nproducer advance with the trap and its architectural write suppressed.\nThe waiting consumer then collects the youngest surviving older value.\nRedirects keep priority. Ordinary aligned producers, including loads\nwith a verified prediction, retain their adjacent bypass timing.\n\nA scratch implementation matched all five CoreMark CRCs in the champion's\n3,044,309 marker cycles. Selftest and all three random retirement traces\nmatched the ISS with both stall generators enabled. All 45 pipeline tests\npassed with exact timing checks for the added fault bubble. The target\nis a median above 96.473 MHz at that cycle count. Independent ALU and\nredirect paths nearly tie the current forwarding path, so the size of\nthe placement gain is uncertain.\n \nhyp-20261121-002-r13s1 Make the collection-to-EX register hold ready-to-use operands. Capture\neach source from its youngest eligible MEM or WB writer, otherwise\nfrom the saved register value, even when the immediate predecessor\nmatches. Register that predecessor's eligible match separately. EX\nselects between the complete fallback and the single registered bypass.\nThus a late alignment check drives a one-bit\nselect flop without gating the 32-bit operand capture. Prepare the\nALU B fallback as a four-way masked OR of immediate, MEM, WB and saved\nrs2. Folding the operand role into these source enables removes a mux\nafter forwarding. Capture AUIPC's existing direct-target sum, PC+4\nfor links, or the LUI immediate in a separate result register. EX can\nthen use rs1 directly as ALU A. Raw rs2 serves stores, branches and RVFI.\n\nThe scratch prototype ran ten CoreMark iterations in 3,044,309 marker\ncycles with both stalls enabled, all five CRCs and the validation banner.\nAll 45 pipeline tests passed. Selftest and the three random RVFI traces\nmatched the ISS with both stalls. In Gowin placement 1, selecting the\nimmediate after the forwarded rs2 mux reached 90.171 MHz. Folding the\nimmediate enable into the four parallel source terms reached 97.596 MHz.\nPlacements 0, 1 and 2 reached 87.381, 97.596 and 97.596 MHz. The median\ngives 320.59 iterations/s, 5.82% above the champion.\n \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
