{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n '\\\"(category|hypothesis_category)\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"predictor\\\"|hyp-20261121-003-r[12]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r1s0 (regression, +42.82%): Testing 15 divisor multiples in parallel raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 7.774 MHz, but chaining eight radix-16 remainder selections in one EX cycle kept the core below the multicycle divider's 43.9 MHz.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r1s1 (improvement, +705.78%): Registering the shared EX divider after every six restoring steps shortened the critical path, and CoreMark incurred no divide stalls because it executed no DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU between timing markers.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.76%): Predicting branches with 32 two-bit counters and steering JALs in fetch avoided one-cycle EX redirects and cut CoreMark cycles by 6.4%, but the combinational EX divider kept Fmax near 5.5 MHz versus 43.9 MHz with multicycle division.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r2s0 (regression, +8.63%): Testing D, 2D and 3D in parallel cut each six-bit divider round from six dependent remainder selections to three, raising Fmax until a path from the register file set the limit.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r2s1 (regression, +5.00%): Splitting at divisor magnitude 2^14 raised Fmax at the same six-round latency because small divisors need only 15-bit trial subtractors and seeding the wide remainder with the top 14 dividend bits cuts the 33-bit subtractor chain from six to three per round.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 (improvement, +9.91%): Storing the control-transfer instruction word in the 64-entry BTB let a tag hit satisfy fetch during imem stalls even when the predictor chose fall-through, saving 154,266 CoreMark cycles over the same BTB with replay disabled.\n4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Predict direct control flow with 32 two-bit counters in fetch\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Fetch currently advances to PC+4 on every accepted instruction. IF/ID is\\ncombinational, so each aligned taken branch or jump resolved in EX costs\\none fetch opportunity. A replay of the canonical CoreMark instruction trace\\nreproduced the basel\n…[14518 of 17590 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:083b19b2e1d99351]…\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 107.34, \"delta_pct\": 9.91, \"vs_baseline\": 785.64, \"fmax_mhz\": 43.402, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4043251, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2985, \"ff\": 669, \"seeds\": [42.784, 43.402, 43.402], \"perturbations\": [[0, 42.784, 35], [1, 43.402, 36], [2, 43.402, 36]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 8, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_0_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -18.373, \"arrival_ns\": 28.668, \"logic_cells\": 183, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 35, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T14:00:11.757030Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 (improvement, +9.91%): Storing the control-transfer instruction word in the 64-entry BTB let a tag hit satisfy fetch during imem stalls even when the predictor chose fall-through, saving 154,266 CoreMark cycles over the same BTB with replay disabled.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
