sion between\n  branches can cause a replay miss, but only an exact PC match can supply an\n  instruction. The ready external response has first priority, then the BTB\n  branch word, then the predicted successor word.\n\n  A scratch RTL prototype completed ten canonical CoreMark iterations in\n  3,511,720 marker cycles with all five CRCs, 13.15% fewer cycles than the\n  champion. Sharing one 16-word sequence between the two directions cost\n  39,471 extra cycles. Separate sequences reached 41.280, 42.159 and\n  42.159 MHz across the three Gowin placement options. The median gives\n  120.05 iterations/s, 11.84% above 107.34. At this cycle count the\n  implementation must exceed 39.429 MHz to clear the acceptance margin.\n  Placement optio\n…[1282 of 4354 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:11faf8c9aa724cea]…\nccessor-word eligibility and\n      resolved taken bits. Reuse its PC, instruction, write and invalidate\n      fields on the existing EX-to-IF connection.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Export advancing and the resolved aligned transfer direction. Use the\n      existing BTB write qualification to identify an anchor. Allow a successor\n      payload write for a decoded legal non-branch, non-jump instruction at an\n      aligned RAM PC on EX advance. FENCE.I invalidation overrides the write.\n      Keep recovery and RVFI next PC driven by the full architectural resolution.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Warm a taken loop, withhold imem on several consecutive successor words\n      and check the cycle of acceptance and the RVFI PC sequence. Change\n      direction, alias two branches to one index and change a JALR target.\n      Check that tag mismatches wait for imem, a dmem hold preserves position,\n      wrong-path stores never issue and FENCE.I exposes replacement code.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
