cycles,\n  with both bus stall generators enabled and all five CRCs correct. Gowin\n  placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 48.079, 50.319 and 50.319 MHz. The median\n  yields 147.50 iterations/s, 5.72 percent above the champion. At this\n  cycle count the acceptance threshold is 49.785 MHz. The same recovery\n  design with 4,096 entries saved only 6,264 further cyc\n…[1867 of 4939 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c0217f74647843f5]…\ning ID/EX snapshot for EX\n      direction and full-target checking, trap handling and FENCE.I recovery.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Require word 17 in the trained loop to advance with imem held low.\n      In the two-word loop, supply a changed body instruction on the second\n      lap and withhold imem from the third. Its write collides with the\n      predicted target read. Check the one-cycle retry and the new value.\n      Exercise two PCs 8 KiB apart, a cold slot in a live group and refill\n      after FENCE.I. For a retargeted JALR behind a held load, check both\n      ready and stalled fetches at the corrected PC, link data, exact RVFI\n      PC pairs and the absence of wrong-path stores.\n  path 1: 26.093 ns, 146 cells, cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_29_s1 -> cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_4_s0\n  path 1: 25.167 ns, 145 cells, cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_29_s1 -> cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_2_s0\n  path 1: 25.167 ns, 145 cells, cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_29_s1 -> cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_2_s0\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
