{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_114", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r7s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-003-r7s2\ntitle: Predict and replay both successors from the source PC\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,399,350 cycles for ten iterations at 57.929 MHz.\n  Round six saved 182,462 cycles with two next-fetch lookups, but its\n  target RAM feedback through the hazard unit nearly tied the divider\n  for the timing limit. The two successors of a conditional share a\n  source PC that is known before its predicted direction is available.\nhypothesis: |\n  Index two synchronous prediction banks by the source instruction PC.\n  One entry describes its fall-through successor, the other its taken\n  successor. Read both at once, then use the registered direction to\n  select the following instruction, its two-bit counter and its target.\n  A trained chain can deliver one word per cycle through adjacent taken\n  branches during an imem wait. Both addresses come from the source PC.\n  This removes the target lookup and hazard decision from the RAM address\n  path during normal issue.\n\n  Register EX's correction and annul the one younger instruction in EX\n  while the corrected PC is already fetching. The pair read for the\n  resolving instruction can supply either outcome on recovery. Train\n  from consecutive valid EX/MEM transfers so fetch-table writes take\n  their PC, instruction and resolved outcome from registered state.\n\n  A scratch prototype using 2,048 fall-through rows and 512 taken rows\n  completed ten iterations in 3,207,645 marker cycles with both bus stall\n  generators and all five CRCs correct. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2\n  reached 56.597, 57.114 and 57.114 MHz, yielding 178.06 iter/s. The\n  acceptance threshold at this cycle count is 57.176 MHz. Placement\n  and the cost of the recovery and replay multiplexers are the main risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the BTB and variable-length path cursors with a fall-through\n      bank indexed by PC[12:2] and a taken bank indexed by PC[10:2].\n      Infer synchronous BSRAM from plain packed vectors. Each payload\n      holds destination PC[19:2], word, counter and control target[19:2].\n      Use a resettable group-valid bit and 16 initialized bits per group\n      per bank. Compare the full destination, including range and alignment,\n      to the effective fetch PC. A ready bus word has priority and must\n      pass the existing control-encoding check before steering fetch.\n      Snapshot both returned candidates across a hold and for the cycle of\n      registered EX correction. A held miss retries its recorded parent\n      index, including after a masked read/write collision. Keep RAM reads\n      independent of combinational downstream stall or redirect. Retain\n      the previous eligible training PC and outcome across bubbles and\n      holds. A valid successor B installs B's word and updated prediction\n      at its predecessor's index and actual direction. Reset and advancing\n      FENCE.I clear validity, saved responses and pending training.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Verify direction and the full resolved target against the ID/EX\n      prediction snapshot. Export the actual direction for recovery.\n      Annul a killed EX instruction's memory effects, forwarding, training,\n      redirect and divider start before it can enter EX/MEM. Carry the hit\n      and counter snapshot into MEM, updating training once on an accepted\n      EX/MEM instruction. Use the registered direct target for branches\n      and JAL, and the resolved next PC for JALR. Retain EX-time FENCE.I\n      invalidation and exclude illegal or uncacheable entries.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Register EX misprediction, resolved PC, source index and actual\n      direction together. On the next cycle select that PC for fetch and\n      kill the younger ID/EX instruction. Suppress its dependency hazard\n      and let decode accept the corrected word immediately if available.\n      Retain the corrected PC across backpressure and preserve the flush\n      needed for a genuine adjacent late-result dependency.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Decode the selected bus or replay data in parallel with the tag\n      check. When a fetch miss or flush inserts a bubble, clear validity\n      and all effectful controls. Preserve ID/EX state on a backend hold.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Train and replay both sides of a conditional, a straight run beyond\n      sixteen words, and adjacent taken jumps. Check the warmed fetch rate,\n      exact RVFI PCs and words, order and store effects. Exercise an index\n      collision, an uninitialized word in a live group, retry on a held\n      collision, a JALR retarget after a stalled load, and FENCE.I with\n      replacement code. Check that a wrong-path store or divide annulled\n      in EX has no effects while the recovery word issues.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r7s2.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(p.stat().st_size)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
