{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith('r5s1'):\n  print(r['motivation']); print(r['changes'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"The champion waits until MEM to issue every load. Even with an idle data\nbus and a ready base register, an immediately dependent branch or second\nload incurs a bubble. The ten-iteration instruction trace contains\n135,320 adjacent load-to-branch register matches and 59,350 adjacent\nload-to-load matches. Giving a load an earlier bus slot can both deliver\nits result to the next instruction and absorb a cycle of memory latency.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Drive io_dmemAddr directly from one clock-enabled 32-bit address\\nregister so Gowin can infer block RAM for the attached memory. Hold\\nit while an older MEM transaction waits. On advance, first reserve\\nthe next slot for an EX store or an EX load that did not complete.\\nOtherwise prepare the decoding instruction's candidate address.\\nRegister grant eligibility when ID advances and qualify use with\\nID/EX.valid, a decoded load, natural alignment and addr[31:20]==0.\\n\\nSelect the youngest nonzero base writer, EX before MEM before the\\nwrite-through register file. An ordinary EX ALU producer can supply\\na zero-displacement address. An accepted EX word load can supply\\nits returned pointer plus the new displacement. A MEM producer can\\nsupply a registered ALU/link value, a previously captured early\\nload result, or the accepted data of an aligned ordinary word load,\\nplus displacement. With no pending writer use rs1 plus the signed\\nI immediate. An unavailable youngest source disqualifies early issue.\\n\\nCapture the raw word, separately formatted byte/half/word result,\\nand completion bit on early acceptance. Use the registered formatted\\nresult on the existing EX/MEM forwarding path. Suppress the load-use\\nbubble only on acceptance. If ready is low, the same request and\\naddress continue into MEM until accepted. A completed early load\\nreleases the bus in MEM even when a younger request sees backpressure.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': \"Expose the ordinary forwarded rs1-plus-immediate address for the\\nolder instruction's reserved slot and the fast ALU result for a\\nzero-offset base dependency. Exclude jumps, unavailable M results\\nand faulting instructions from the EX fast-base case.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Latch the ID/EX payload on a decode advance. Apply squash and reset\\nto the valid bit and side-effect controls independently of the wide\\noperand payload, keeping the late load acceptance decision off those\\ndata inputs. Hold both on backpressure.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'For an early-completed load, use its saved raw word with the original\\neffective address, width and sign for MEM/WB and RVFI. Suppress its\\nsecond bus request and stall. Use normal MEM handshakes for fallback\\nloads and all stores, preserving byte masks, misalignment traps,\\nMMIO ordering and one channel-zero retirement per instruction.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Count accepted transactions and check uninterrupted EX/MEM forwarding\\nfor LW-to-branch and LW-to-load, including a nonzero displacement on\\na returned pointer. Exercise byte and halfword sign extension, a denied\\nearly read held through MEM, a stalled older store, an unavailable M\\nbase, two writers to the same base, a flushed load and a misaligned\\nload. Check exact bus addresses, masks, RVFI data and order. Assert\\nthe original bubble on fallback and adjacent retirement on an early hit.\\n'}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
