{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'for n in ph px; do tail -3 \"$TMPDIR/load/${n}_timing/gowin_p1/gw.log\"; done\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r8s2.yaml | head -39'","aggregated_output":"[30%] Placement Phase 2 completed\n[50%] Placement Phase 3 completed\nRunning routing......\n[10%] Placement Phase 0 completed\n[20%] Placement Phase 1 completed\n[30%] Placement Phase 2 completed\nid: hyp-20261121-003-r8s2\ntitle: Predict the effective-address carry to replay loads during RAM waits\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  A marker-bracketed trace of the champion counted 191,317 data-bus stall\n  cycles, 45,890 redirects and 19,787 cycles without a fetch word over ten\n  CoreMark iterations. The 544,852 loads give a word-address predictor a\n  larger opportunity than further improvements to branch direction. A\n  PC-stride load predictor saved only 39,881 cycles in a scratch run.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict the carry into effective-address bit 6 to start a synchronous\n  load-word lookup in EX. Form the low six address bits and the next six\n  bits in parallel. Use displacement bit 5 as the predicted carry between\n  the slices. This predicts zero carry for small positive offsets and one\n  for small negative offsets. A zero offset gives the exact index even\n  when the base is a freshly loaded pointer. The 1,024-entry RAM stores\n  raw words observed on the data bus and their address tags.\n\n  Register the predicted index beside the RAM read. In parallel, compute\n  the exact low address bits for the external bus by using the actual\n  carry to select either upper-slice sum. Give these bits their own\n  EX/MEM register. In MEM, qualify the word with its valid bit, full address,\n  ordinary-RAM range, natural alignment and write-collision status. An\n  accepted bus read supplies the live word. During backpressure a\n  verified prediction can supply the same word and complete the load.\n  A wrong carry or tag costs the usual memory wait. Full-word stores\n  install their data and partial stores invalidate the indexed word.\n\n  A scratch RTL prototype took 3,078,813 marker cycles versus 3,223,900\n  for the champion with both stall generators, all five canonical CRCs\n  and the validation banner. This saves 145,087 cycles. It needs median\n  Gowin Fmax above 60.6763 MHz to clear 197.07686 iterations/s. That\n  narrow timing margin is the main risk. The version using the general\n  ALU result for the external address reached 59.588 MHz median and\n  193.54 iterations/s. Its worst path on placement 1 ran from a WB\n  register identifier through EX forwarding and the ALU to data RAM.\n  Registering the corrected low address separately targets that path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
