{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_91", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r9s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-003-r9s2\ntitle: Predict the load word during operand collection and verify it before consumption\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion executes 544,852 loads in 3,273,911 marker cycles. Its\n  adjacent LW-to-pointer and load-to-branch paths both consume live MEM\n  data in EX. Round eight's predicted-index word replay saved 145,087\n  cycles on its parent, but still sent the MEM response through those\n  bypasses. The champion's operand-collection stage offers a full extra\n  cycle to look up a load before either consumer needs its value.\nhypothesis: |\n  Start a synchronous, PC-assisted word lookup as a load leaves operand\n  collection. Predict the base from the youngest cheap operand source.\n  For consecutive pointer loads, use the preceding lookup's raw word\n  directly as the candidate base. Form the low six address bits by addition.\n  Predict word-index bits [12:6] by XORing the candidate base with the\n  change observed at the last execution of the same instruction. The\n  instruction replay row already has seven spare successor bits on a\n  sequential instruction. Its low eleven successor bits still steer fetch.\n\n  In EX, validate the candidate against the architectural base and the\n  entire addressed word, including RAM range, alignment and intervening\n  writes. Register the raw word for retirement and the extended load\n  value for the adjacent consumer. A verified hit completes the load\n  internally. On a miss, MEM requests the exact external address. An\n  independent younger instruction proceeds when that transaction completes.\n  A dependent instruction holds in EX, captures the accepted operand and\n  executes on the following cycle. This takes live data RAM off the\n  immediate load-to-branch and load-to-address paths.\n\n  An isolated RTL prototype completed ten iterations in 3,139,707 marker\n  cycles with both stalls, all five expected CRCs and the validation banner.\n  It saved 134,204 cycles. At that cycle count the acceptance threshold is\n  71.733 MHz median. A prototype with the replay-hit signal in the operand\n  bypass select reached 68.996 MHz on placement 1. Register the candidate\n  forwarding value and the producer selection before the consumer's EX\n  stage. Use verification to authorize EX advance and side effects.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry a seven-bit address XOR mask in the prediction snapshot and the EX training transaction.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Store the mask in successor[19:13] of a sequential replay row.\n      Preserve successor[12:2] for the link walker, the full target on a\n      control row, the buffered instruction's snapshot and FENCE.I\n      invalidation. Supply zero on a cold lookup.\n  - file: rtl/load_predictor.sv\n    description: |\n      Use a 2,048-row synchronous RAM holding raw words, valid bits and\n      address tags [19:13]. Carry the selected index, candidate base and\n      read eligibility with the load. Compare the true forwarded base with\n      the candidate and compare candidate-base-plus-immediate with the\n      complete tag and index. Honor byte and halfword alignment and use\n      the addressed lane for extension. Register equality in independent\n      slices. Install accepted ordinary reads and full-word stores.\n      Invalidate colliding partial stores. Reject read/write collisions\n      on both edges between lookup and use, including a held lookup.\n      Reset eligibility immediately and sweep validity while misses use\n      the bus. An outstanding bus miss holds its address until acceptance.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Start the lookup from the waiting slot. Select an unverified preceding\n      LW word for a pointer chain, an older registered ALU or load candidate,\n      WB data, or the saved base. Latch metadata only with its instruction.\n      Let an adjacent consumer enter EX behind a load. If the load misses,\n      hold that consumer and the front end, drain the accepted load once,\n      inject an EX/MEM bubble and replace matching operands with accepted\n      data. A misaligned producer preserves the saved older operand. Verify\n      both source matches, x0, reset, flush and divider ownership. Keep\n      external requests on exact registered addresses, with writes and\n      MMIO following the existing handshakes.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Train the mask from the actual base and effective address of an\n      advancing memory instruction. Capture the formatted candidate in the\n      same forwarding register used for the preceding ALU or link result.\n      A dependent instruction can compute from that prediction while MEM\n      verifies it. Gate redirect, divide start, predictor training and the\n      EX/MEM transfer on successful validation or completed operand repair.\n      Preserve the raw word, exact address, byte masks and single retirement\n      for RVFI.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Include the predictor in the pipeline test's RTL source list. Compare\n      cold and warmed pointer chains, load-dependent branches and subword\n      ALU consumers. Force a wrong mask, a same-index different tag, stores\n      on each lookup edge, a partial store and a stalled bus miss. Check the\n      retry issues no duplicate transaction or retirement, wrong-path stores\n      stay squashed, and a faulting load preserves the previous writer.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r9s2.yaml');j=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(j,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));print(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
