ith the\n      complete tag and index. Honor byte and halfword alignment and use\n      the addressed lane for extension. Register equality in independent\n      slices. Install accepted ordinary reads and full-word stores.''','''      address tags [19:13]. Carry the selected index, lane and eligibility\n      with the load. At EX/MEM register the expected byte address as\n      {12'b0, row_tag, read_index, lane}, the raw word and lookup validity.\n      Format byte, halfword and word candidates from the saved lane,\n      width and sign control. Qualify the MEM comparison with validity,\n      load legality and natural alignment. Install accepted ordinary-RAM\n      reads and full-word stores.''')\ns=s.replace('''      external requests on exact registered addresses, with writes and\n      MMIO following the existing handshakes.''','''      external requests on exact addresses. Compute low address candidates\n      for the collected base and the adjacent forwarded value, select the\n      true sum into a dedicated register for port bits [12:2], and hold it\n      with EX/MEM. Stores and MMIO use their existing handshakes.''')\ns=s.replace('''      for RVFI.''','''      for RVFI. Use the registered candidate in the consumer datapath\n      independently of the tag comparison. On a miss, suppress all of that\n      consumer's effects until MEM supplies its correct operand.''')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r9s2.yaml');j=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(j,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));print(j['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Start a synchronous, PC-assisted word lookup as a load leaves operand\ncollection. Predict the base from the youngest cheap operand source.\nFor consecutive pointer loads, use the preceding lookup's raw word\ndirectly as the candidate base. Form the low six address bits by addition.\nPredict word-index bits [12:6] by XORing the candidate base with the\nchange observed at the last execution of the same instruction. The\ninstruction replay row already has seven spare successor bits on a\nsequential instruction. Its low eleven successor bits still steer fetch.\n\nIn EX, format the candidate and register its raw word, extended value\nand expected byte address. Build that address from the returned row tag,\nthe actual RAM read index and the two lane bits used for formatting.\nIn MEM compare it with the registered, exact 32-bit effective address.\nThis single comparison checks the base prediction, learned mask, tag\nand lane together. A verified hit completes the load\ninternally. On a miss, MEM requests the exact external address. An\nindependent younger instruction proceeds when that transaction completes.\nA dependent instruction holds in EX, captures the accepted operand and\nexecutes on the following cycle. This takes live data RAM off the\nimmediate load-to-branch and load-to-address paths.\n\nAn isolated RTL prototype completed ten iterations in 3,139,707 marker\ncycles with both stalls, all five expected CRCs and the validation banner.\nIt saved 134,204 cycles. At that cycle count acceptance requires a median\nabove 71.73204 MHz. With the full address comparison in MEM\nand the candidate already in the EX/MEM forwarding register, Gowin\nplacement 1 reached 72.335 MHz, equivalent to 230.39 iterations/s.\nSelftest and all three random programs matched the reference retirement\ntraces under both stalls. Median timing determines acceptance.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
