{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r15s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-001-r15s0\ntitle: Resolve ordered branches with parallel byte comparisons\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,044,309 cycles to retire 2,922,016 instructions\n  between the CoreMark markers. Even perfect single issue would gain only\n  4.19% at 97.260 MHz. Gowin placement 0 reports a 37-cell path from bit 2\n  of the adjacent result register to the decode valid register. An ordered\n  branch on that result currently puts a full-width magnitude comparison\n  between forwarding and the redirect that clears decode.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the EX branch comparison into four independent byte slices. Each\n  slice computes unsigned less-than and equality on the forwarded rs1 and\n  rs2. Combine two adjacent slices as lt_hi OR (eq_hi AND lt_lo), then\n  combine the two halfwords the same way. For the most significant slice,\n  differing sign bits decide signed order directly. Equal signs use the\n  ordinary magnitude result. Reduce the four equality bits for BEQ/BNE.\n  Select equality or ordering with funct3 and invert for BNE, BGE or BGEU.\n\n  This makes propagation from bit 2 to branch recovery traverse one byte\n  comparator and two combine levels. The same exact branch condition drives\n  prediction training, next PC and recovery on the existing EX edge. The\n  expected cycle count is 3,044,309, so promotion requires a median above\n  101.73 MHz. The main risk is another EX path setting the clock period.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the six-way branch condition case with a balanced comparison\n      of four byte pairs. Use the existing forwarded rs1 and rs2 for every\n      slice, including after a load repair. Preserve the resolved taken bit,\n      alignment fault behavior, redirect qualification and training enables.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
