pplies the exact result to WB and older\n  writer forwarding. An independent successor advances immediately.\n  If an adjacent consumer selected an unfinished shift, use the existing\n  load-repair hold to replace only its matching source or sources before\n  it can execute, redirect, start division or access memory. Hold all\n  shift metadata with its producer on backpressure. Keep load verification\n  and this completion condition distinct.\n\n  A scratch prototype that sent every distance of eight or more through\n  MEM took 3,082,664 marker cycles. Adding the three direct immediate\n  distances reduced that to 3,044,495, only 186 cycles above the champion.\n  Both runs used both stall generators and produced all five canonical\n  CRCs and the validation banner. At the latter count promotion requires\n  a median above 101.74 MHz. The timing hypothesis is that collection\n  can absorb the full route decode and shorten the EX result path enough\n  to reach that clock.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Isolate the shift-distance input from operand B. Support a three-bit fine shift in the pipeline while retaining full-width standalone ALU behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Register byte-route enables from the decoded immediate shift, qualify the fine result selects, and extend the existing adjacent-source repair logic to unfinished shift producers.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Combine the selected fixed byte wiring or fine shift with the ordinary result. Register the coarse count, direction, sign-fill control and completion flag on the EX/MEM transfer.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Finish deferred shifts on the registered partial word and deliver the exact value on both the WB and MEM forwarding paths.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check all 32 distances for both immediate and forwarded register shifts, negative SRA operands, dual-source dependencies, repair under backpressure and an independent successor.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport tempfile, os\nscratch=p.with_suffix('.writing')\ndata=yaml.safe_load(s)\njsonschema.validate(data,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nscratch.write_text(s)\nos.replace(scratch,p)\nprint(p, 319.48*1.046*3044495/1e7)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r15s1.yaml 101.73974046796\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
