{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('round_id',0) in [] or d['id'].endswith(('r13s2','r14s2','r14s0','r13s0','r13s1')):\n  print(d['id'],d.get('hypothesis'), d['critical_path'], d['seeds'],d['cycles'],d['ipc_coremark'], d['bsram'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r13s0 {'motivation': \"On the champion's 92.229 MHz Gowin placement, a path from bit 0 of\\nEX/MEM.alu_result to bit 24 of the next collected rs1 arrives at\\n16.141 ns. It traverses the forwarded base, the low address adder,\\nalignment checking and ex_writer before selecting a 32-bit operand.\\nOther destinations on that path include collected rs2. The tag match\\nand the producer's decoded write intent are both known a cycle earlier.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Record the two adjacent RAW matches when a producer moves from\\ncollection into EX and the following instruction moves from decode into\\ncollection. For each source compare its decode address to the producer's\\nnonzero rd and qualify the match with producer validity and decoded\\nreg_write. Drive operand selection from those registered matches and EX\\nvalidity. This removes address generation and trap checking from the\\npath that zeros the saved value and selects the adjacent bypass.\\n\\nA load or link instruction can still lose its write permission in EX.\\nIf its data or link alignment check fails and a waiting source matches,\\nuse the existing late-result interlock for one issue bubble. Let the\\nproducer advance with the trap and its architectural write suppressed.\\nThe waiting consumer then collects the youngest surviving older value.\\nRedirects keep priority. Ordinary aligned producers, including loads\\nwith a verified prediction, retain their adjacent bypass timing.\\n\\nA scratch implementation matched all five CoreMark CRCs in the champion's\\n3,044,309 marker cycles. Selftest and all three random retirement traces\\nmatched the ISS with both stall generators enabled. All 45 pipeline tests\\npassed with exact timing checks for the added fault bubble. The target\\nis a median above 96.473 MHz at that cycle count. Independent ALU and\\nredirect paths nearly tie the current forwarding path, so the size of\\nthe placement gain is uncertain.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description'\n…[16722 of 19794 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d2a479e5361ab82a]…\ne fully forwarded operands\\nand the existing mismatch, trap and redirect decisions.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register actual outcome and both counter candidates with the EX\\nfill. Select the counter and use its MSB to prepare both the row counter\\nand its successor so they always describe the same prediction.\\nOrdinary rows, jumps, replay qualification and FENCE.I use the\\nexisting fill and lookup rules.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Train a repeated eight-continuation loop, then change its trip\\ncount. Check that the warm final continuation predicts the exit,\\nthat a wrong count recovers to the architectural PC, and that\\neach store commits once. Cover the forward-exit form, a saturated\\ncount and a held branch with an older stalled load.\\n'}]} {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/fill_control_s0', 'slack_ns': -5.603, 'arrival_ns': 15.897, 'logic_cells': 34, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex']} [94.311, 91.955, 91.955] 3009439 3e-06 25\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
