{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml && python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith('r11s2'): print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][:1970])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 97.26\n  lut4: 4883\n  ff: 1934\n  coremark_iter_s: 3.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261121-003-r13s2\n  updated: '2026-11-21T22:59:53.940748Z'\nGive each load two reads of a coherent resident-page word RAM. As the\nload leaves collection, predict the word index from the current base and\ndisplacement. For a pointer chain, use the preceding load's unverified\nword as the next base guess. In EX format the predicted word using the\nreal byte offset and capture it in the ordinary EX/MEM forwarding register.\nIn parallel, check the actual word index, RAM page, initialization and\nfreshness. The next instruction may execute from the registered candidate\nwhile MEM qualifies it. A verified hit removes both the bus wait and the\nadjacent load-use bubble.\n\nStart the second read in EX at the exact forwarded address. It rescues\nan incorrect early guess without issuing an external read. Capture late\neligibility in EX using an initialized-sector bit. Require every word in\nthe sector to be known before enabling this shortcut. Independently\ninitialized words can still satisfy the early probe. If an adjacent\nconsumer used an incorrect early prediction, annul its effects, hold\nit in EX, and capture the verified late value or the accepted bus value\ninto each matching operand. Re-execute it once. Independent consumers\ncontinue as soon as the load completes.\n\nIn a scratch implementation this took 3,045,213 marker cycles with both\nstall generators, saving 193,216 cycles (5.97%) and matching all five\nCRCs and the validation banner. That cycle count needs a median above\n82.07 MHz to exceed 269.50 iterations/s. The initial three-placement\nmedian was 78.274 MHz. Its worst path ran from a forwarded operand to\nfront-end flush. Shorten verification of a predicted JALR consuming that\noperand by comparing its base against the expected base computed in\ncollection. This keeps the full target adder off the flush decision.\nForm each EX operand by ORing its saved value with the enabled bypass.\nZero the saved value on issue only when a qualified adjacent writer\nsupplies that source. On repair, capture the verified value \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
