{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_90","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r15s2.yaml')\np.write_text(\\\"\\\"\\\"id: hyp-20261122-003-r15s2\ntitle: Predict the next PC before the replay tag check completes\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion retires 2,922,016 instructions in 3,044,309 CoreMark\n  marker cycles. Perfect issue at its current clock would gain 4.19%,\n  below the 4.6% promotion margin. The replay tag and initialized-bit\n  checks currently qualify both the instruction word and the predicted\n  direction. Only the instruction word needs that proof before issue.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use the replay row's control bit, counter MSB and stored successor as\n  a speculative next-PC prediction. For steering, qualify the row with\n  the registered live_q or the buffered-word flag. Allow a row-index\n  or tag alias to predict the destination of an externally supplied\n  legal control instruction. Carry the actual direction and target\n  used by fetch in the instruction's prediction snapshot so EX can\n  correct either a wrong direction or a wrong JALR destination.\n  Keep prediction.hit exact for counter training.\n  \n  The instruction data contract stays precise. An available external\n  word wins, its control opcode qualifies steering, and a stalled imem\n  supplies an instruction only through the existing full-PC, initialized\n  replay hit or a previously verified buffer. A false hint alone cannot\n  advance a stalled fetch. Initialize stored hints to not-taken at FPGA\n  configuration so an unwritten row cannot select an unknown target.\n  Preserve the live-bit suppression on read/write collisions, reset,\n  redirects and FENCE.I. Every speculative target remains word-aligned\n  and within the existing RAM fetch range.\n  \n  A scratch implementation completed ten iterations with both stall\n  generators, all five canonical CRCs and the validation banner in\n  3,044,787 marker cycles, 478 more than the champion. The proposed\n  gain comes from taking the full row check off the PC steering path.\n  At that measured cycle count the median must exceed 101.75 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compute prediction.taken from (buffered || live_q), word.control,\n      word.counter[1] and the existing external-control qualification.\n      Continue using the full hit for prediction.hit and for replay word\n      admission. Give the predictor a deterministic cold not-taken state\n      while retaining synchronous block RAM inference.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Train a taken jump and visit an externally supplied branch at an\n      alias with a different target. Check the resolved PC, consecutive\n      RVFI orders and exactly one correct-path store. Stall imem on the\n      mismatched row and verify that its cached instruction cannot issue.\n      Exercise recovery with a buffered word and FENCE.I.\n\\\"\\\"\\\")\nPY\ncat \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/steer/test_result.log\" | tail -9 && tail -5 \"$TMPDIR/steer/p1/gw.log\" && date -u'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
