{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r15s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20261122-003-r15s2\ntitle: Steer fetch with a four-bit PC match and verify replay words separately\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion retires 2,922,016 instructions in 3,044,309 CoreMark marker\n  cycles. Even perfect issue at 97.260 MHz would gain only 4.19%, below\n  the 4.6% promotion margin. Today a taken prediction waits for the\n  replay row's full PC comparison and the dynamic selection of one of\n  sixteen initialized bits. Fetch needs both checks to issue a cached\n  instruction. EX can recover a speculative target using the existing\n  direction and target checks.\nhypothesis: |\n  Check only PC bits [5:2] against the replay read index when using a\n  row as a next-PC hint. Keep the full PC comparison for supplying\n  instruction data and reporting prediction.hit. This lets a ready\n  external branch or jump use a hint while its full tag is being\n  checked. A buffered, previously verified word can supply its hint\n  directly. Snapshot the actual taken bit and target in the usual\n  prediction bundle, including on a partial match that misses the full\n  tag, so EX can recover at the existing misprediction latency.\n\n  Select the addressed initialized bit at the synchronous read edge.\n  Register it with the replay row and its index, hold all three together\n  during buffering, and retain live_q's collision and invalidation\n  rules. At fill, encode the counter MSB as fill_control AND the trained\n  counter MSB. Every ordinary instruction thus carries a zero steering\n  hint. On a ready response, retain the external opcode check. A stalled\n  imem can issue only a verified replay word. Aliasing can change the\n  predicted fetch address, but cannot authorize a cached instruction.\n\n  A scratch prototype passed all 46 pipeline tests and completed ten\n  CoreMark iterations with both stall generators, all five canonical\n  CRCs and the validation banner. It took 3,044,442 marker cycles,\n  133 more than the champion. Promotion at that count requires a median\n  above 101.738 MHz. The remaining uncertainty is whether shortening\n  fetch steering improves the clock before an independent EX path limits it.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture initialized[read_index[12:6]][read_index[5:2]] as known_q\n      on the row read enable. Use known_q in the exact row_hit. Permit\n      steering on buffered OR (live_q AND known_q AND index_q[5:2] equal\n      to pc[5:2]). Combine this with the prequalified counter MSB and\n      the existing external-control check. Preserve exact replay validity,\n      full-tag prediction.hit, fill timing and FENCE.I invalidation.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Train a taken control at P and present a ready JALR at P+0x2000\n      with a different target. Arrange for the aliased row to be probed.\n      Verify recovery from its stale target and exactly one correct-path\n      store. With imemReady low at the alias, require the PC to hold and\n      the cached instruction to stay out of retirement.\nEOF\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r15s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']==p.stem and all((Path('cores/bench')/c['file']).is_file() for c in d['changes'])\nprint('Validated',p,'with',len(d['changes']),'target-local changes')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
